payload_content.text:
Fix the MCP transport/restart architecture without depending on a stable current MCP session.

Current facts:

- &#x20;Local MCP server is healthy on `127.0.0.1:3000`.&#x20;
- &#x20;Tailscale Funnel points `https://kone.tailbf0440.ts.net` to that local listener.&#x20;
- &#x20;After the recent listener recycle, ChatGPT workers intermittently get `Connection failed` / refresh-action 502s before requests reach the local MCP server.&#x20;
- &#x20;MCP calls may succeed, then the next call disconnect, then succeed again after rediscovery.&#x20;
- &#x20;Do **not** interpret these connector disconnects as task failure.&#x20;

Work autonomously despite disconnects:

- &#x20;Preserve the exact task, branch/worktree, BUSY scope, dirty state, and every `process_id`.&#x20;
- &#x20;If an MCP call disconnects after `start_process`, rediscover MCP0 through the generic connector registry and `read_output` from the **same process\_id**. Never start a duplicate merely because the read disconnected.&#x20;
- &#x20;Do not fall back to Commander just because one MCP call disconnects.&#x20;
- &#x20;Keep individual shell operations bounded and checkpoint important findings to files/Git so a connector drop does not lose progress.&#x20;
- &#x20;Do not restart the live MCP listener again while implementing the fix.&#x20;

Goal:\
&#x20;Make deployment/restarts stop disrupting the public ChatGPT MCP endpoint. Investigate and implement the safest architecture, preferably a stable front door/proxy whose public TCP endpoint remains continuously alive while MCP backends can be replaced behind it. The current backend is hard-coded to `127.0.0.1:3000`, so adapt that constraint safely if needed and test backend instances on alternate loopback ports before any live cutover.

Requirements:

- &#x20;Inspect `AGENTS.md`, `keepalive.ps1`, `start.ps1`, `src/index.ts`, Tailscale Funnel configuration, supervisor behavior, and restart-continuity tests.&#x20;
- &#x20;Build and test changes off the live path first.&#x20;
- &#x20;Add regression proof that a backend replacement does not make the public/front-door health endpoint disappear.&#x20;
- &#x20;Preserve OAuth/store/BUSY/process state correctly.&#x20;
- &#x20;No destructive cleanup and no listener recycle until a zero/near-zero-downtime cutover is proven.&#x20;
- &#x20;If the connector drops during your work, recover and continue automatically; do not stop merely because the chat lost MCP for a tu

