Transport-log growth as cause of multi-second stalls: NOT_PROVEN.\n- Upstream/client pre-dispatch routing or authorization failure as a distinct class: SUPPORTED, not yet PROVEN for a fresh timestamp-correlated MCP-active incident.\n\n## Closure gate\nKeep this issue open until a fresh user-visible MCP failure occurs during a proven MCP-active interval and the narrow matching telemetry window is captured. The incident is closure-grade only if it records: exact local timestamp, whether `/mcp` reached the server, completion/close/abort/non-2xx state and `response_bytes` when present, localhost and public/Funnel health, and any intentional revoke/restart/route switch/process kill. If no fresh failure occurs, the current implementation and classification framework are complete but the intermittent upstream/non-arrival attribution remains SUPPORTED rather than PROVEN.","comments":[{"id":"IC_kwDOUBs2L88AAAABQkxBGg","author":{"login":"organicoverlords"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"Historical Commander corpus first pass: DesktopCommanderFallback/remote.log.1 is 291,258,422 bytes. Streaming scan found 59 occurrences of 'transport failure', 45 'socket=closed', 51 'Channel error', 30 'Channel subscribed', 28 online transitions, and 27 offline transitions. This is an independent transport implementation showing repeated transport disconnect/recovery behavior. Caveat: these are Commander transport errors, not yet evidence of ChatGPT pre-dispatch safety blocks; timestamp/call correlation is still required. Current MCP corpus separately rejects a hard 6 KB ceiling and fixed call-count limit.","createdAt":"2026-08-25T07:55:58Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/organicoverlords/chatgpt-mcp-clean/issues/7#issuecomment-5407260954","viewerDidAuthor":true},{"id":"IC_kwDOUBs2L88AAAABQkxlTQ","author":{"login":"organicoverlords"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"Version timeline established from Gi