ure remains SUPPORTED as a distinct class but requires timestamp-correlated MCP-active incidents.\n\nThe file also defines the capture contract for the next visible failure: exact timestamp -> matching `/mcp` boundary event -> response outcome/`response_bytes` -> local/public health -> intentional switch/revoke/restart check -> classify or leave NOT_PROVEN.\n\nI am leaving #7 open because the classification framework is now durable, but the random upstream/non-arrival condition itself is not eliminated or conclusively attributed.","createdAt":"2026-08-25T17:52:25Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/organicoverlords/chatgpt-mcp-clean/issues/7#issuecomment-5414464043","viewerDidAuthor":true},{"id":"IC_kwDOUBs2L88AAAABQrqchg","author":{"login":"organicoverlords"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"Operationalized the #7 failure split in the repo incident workflow. Commit `85dea3d` adds an MCP boundary-classification section to `workflows/incident-report/SKILL.md`: capture the exact timestamp, prove MCP was active, check whether `/mcp` reached the local server, record completion/abort/non-2xx plus `response_bytes`, correlate localhost vs public/Funnel health, and account for intentional revoke/restart/route-switch events before assigning A/B/C/D/E. This prevents future incidents from being collapsed into a generic \"MCP died\" diagnosis. Remaining closure condition: capture at least one new user-visible failure during a proven MCP-active interval and classify it from the matching boundary telemetry; otherwise the upstream/pre-dispatch attribution remains SUPPORTED rather than PROVEN.","createdAt":"2026-08-25T17:55:00Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/organicoverlords/chatgpt-mcp-clean/issues/7#issuecomment-5414493318","viewerDidAuthor":true}],"number":7,"title":"Investigate intermittent ChatGPT pre-dispatch 