65:{"kind":"correction","scope":"mcp","tags":["incident","regression","rate-comparison","rollback"],"title":"MCP reproduction does not prove unchanged regression rate","text":"2026-08-27 incident correction: while deciding whether MCP c2fa477 was worse, the assistant reproduced the same pre-server failure class on a preserved older server under current surrounding state, then incorrectly used that bounded reproduction to say the current build was not worse and to block rollback. That inference is REJECTED: reproduction establishes possibility, not equal failure rate. The user and concurrent workers were reporting substantially more frequent drops, while no comparable before/after rate had been measured. Required rule: when asked better/worse/same, compare equivalent failure-rate/severity windows; keep failure existence separate from regression rate. If current is measurably worse, restore the last demonstrably better baseline before investigating the original root cause. Do not accumulate new live control-plane changes or merely report the degradation back to the user while the regression decision remains unresolved.","state":"PROVEN","evidence":["report:01 Reports/2026-08-27_0010_EEST_mcp-rate-comparison-invalid-inference_incident_report.md","user-correction:2026-08-27"],"supersedes":[],"id":"mem-20260827-cecc8a66","timestamp":"2026-08-27T00:36:28+03:00"}
74:{"kind":"correction","scope":"mcp","tags":["incident","slopwall","measurement","non-arrival","regression"],"title":"Successful MCP arrivals cannot measure non-arrival reliability","text":"2026-08-27 slopwall incident: while comparing old/new MCP reliability, the assistant used server response logs and said per-active-session call rate was roughly unchanged. That metric was invalid because the proven pre-dispatch `Connection failed` events often never reach 3003 and are absent from server logs. User screenshots then showed repeated failures during ordinary worker source/audit work, not just synthetic probes. Contributing causes: observability bias toward precise server telemetry, premature quantitative closure, anchoring on the concurrency explanation, and correction-regurgitation instead of completing the regression decision. Required rule: for non-arrival failures, client/worker-visible attempts, explicit failures, rediscoveries, and completions are the reliability denominator; server logs only classify where failed attempts disappeared. Do not declare better/same/worse or block rollback from censored arrival data.","state":"PROVEN","evidence":["report:01 Reports/2026-08-27_0108_EEST_mcp-successful-arrivals-denominator-slopwall_incident_report.md","conversation-screenshots:2026-08-27"],"supersedes":[],"id":"mem-20260827-807066be","timestamp":"2026-08-27T01:10:31+03:00"}
75:{"kind":"lesson","scope":"mcp","tags":["slopwall","rate-comparison","causal-inference"],"title":"SLOPWALL 2026-08-27 - spam versus concurrency causal oscillation","text":"SLOPWALL incident 2026-08-27: assistant oscillated from calling the current MCP traffic model spam to calling session/concurrency explosion the real culprit. The second claim still exceeded the evidence. Observed: quiet cd3be1b window had 577 tool calls over about 8.3h with 5 non-null session fingerprints plus one null-session caller; current front-door window had 2,746 calls over about 2.8h with 13 non-null session fingerprints plus one null-session caller. caller_id is derived from x-openai-session, then mcp-session-id, then authorization; 2,707/2,746 current calls had a matching non-null session fingerprint. However, the windows were not workload-controlled, so more active sessions can reflect more intentionally running workers rather than a regression. Front-door request-ID duplication was separately rejected for the logged sample. Specific Connection failed events with no matching front_request_start remain pre-dispatch/non-arrival and do not isolate ChatGPT connector versus Funnel/public path. Provisional contributing causes: premature convergence, confirmation pressure after the user challenged the prior conclusion, failure to control worker count/task mix, and treating a traffic decomposition as a causal diagnosis. Keep request amplification, per-session behavior, and pre-dispatch failure source separate until each is isolated.","state":"PROVISIONAL","evidence":["conversation:2026-08-27-current-chat"],"supersedes":[],"id":"mem-20260827-bd390966","timestamp":"2026-08-27T01:10:42+03:00"}
