esson\", \"scope\": \"mcp\", \"tags\": [\"routing\", \"safety\", \"non-arrival\", \"classifier\"], \"text\": \"A ChatGPT MCP failure with zero corresponding server arrival is a different failure class from a locally observed transport/server failure; do not diagnose zero-arrival as local server death or hammer retries.\", \"state\": \"PROVEN\", \"evidence\": [\"github:organicoverlords/chatgpt-mcp-clean#7\"], \"supersedes\": [\"mem-20260825-mcp-6kb-hard\"]}, {\"kind\": \"lesson\", \"scope\": \"mcp\", \"tags\": [\"slopwall\", \"rate-comparison\", \"causal-inference\"], \"title\": \"SLOPWALL 2026-08-27 - spam versus concurrency causal oscillation\", \"text\": \"SLOPWALL incident 2026-08-27: assistant oscillated from calling the current MCP traffic model spam to calling session/concurrency explosion the real culprit. The second claim still exceeded the evidence. Observed: quiet cd3be1b window had 577 tool calls over about 8.3h with 5 non-null session fingerprints plus one null-session caller; current front-door window had 2,746 calls over about 2.8h with 13 non-null session fingerprints plus one null-session caller. caller_id is derived from x-openai-session, then mcp-session-id, then authorization; 2,707/2,746 current calls had a matching non-null session fingerprint. However, the windows were not workload-controlled, so more active sessions can reflect more intentionally running workers rather than a regression. Front-door request-ID duplication was separately rejected for the logged sample. Specific Connection failed events with no matching front_request_start remain pre-dispatch/non-arrival and do not isolate ChatGPT connector versus Funnel/public path. Provisional contributing causes: premature convergence, confirmation pressure after the user challenged the prior conclusion, failure to control worker count/task mix, and treating a traffic decomposition as a causal diagnosis. Keep request amplification, per-session behavior, and pre-dispatch failure source separate