ting direct reuse. Root cause remains NOT_PROVEN.\",\"state\":\"PROVEN\",\"evidence\":[],\"supersedes\":[],\"id\":\"mem-20260826-d4d27626\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-08-26T23:48:02+03:00\"}\r\n{\"kind\":\"fact\",\"scope\":\"mcp\",\"tags\":[\"mcp\",\"ab-test\",\"tool-transition\",\"namespace\",\"pre-3003\"],\"title\":\"2026-08-26 A/B same-tool versus alternating-tool MCP test\",\"text\":\"2026-08-26 ~22:48-22:52 EEST, PR #16 c2fa477 live. A: busy_list x20 = 20/20 PASS, no rediscovery. B: start_process -> read_output x20 = 18 clean pairs plus 2 Connection failed events. B06: process 1c5a5681-d837-43eb-83b1-fac1b09336dc started 22:49:54.741, exited 22:49:55.007; first read_output failed before 3003, MCP0 remained directly callable, no refresh was done, and exact same read reached front 22:50:05.603/backend process_read 22:50:05.609 and succeeded. B16: B15 read succeeded 22:51:38.293; next start_process returned Connection failed with no returned pid; immediate direct busy_list succeeded, so namespace loss was not coupled to the network failure. During B, client initialize/initialized exchanges occurred automatically at 22:49:54.350/.437 and 22:51:37.912/38.000 without explicit list_resources. Conclusions: pre-3003 failure reproduced; execution-state loss rejected; namespace disappearance is a separate phenomenon; tool-transition bug is PLAUSIBLE, NOT_PROVEN.\",\"state\":\"PROVEN\",\"evidence\":[],\"supersedes\":[],\"id\":\"mem-20260826-78d10d87\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-08-26T23:48:13+03:00\"}\r\n{\"kind\":\"correction\",\"scope\":\"orchestration\",\"tags\":[\"busy\",\"mcp\",\"control-plane\",\"ownership\"],\"title\":\"MCP BUSY is authoritative live ownership\",\"text\":\"2026-08-26 control-plane correction: MCP0 BUSY claim state is the sole live ownership authority for shared mutation. GitHub issue BUSY titles are human-visible projections only and cannot establish ownership. If the matching MCP claim is absent, the GitHub BUSY marker is stale and must not block work. Workers must busy_list then busy_claim exact scope before mutation, and busy_release immediately when mutation stops/switches/handoffs. This supersedes the earlier direction that GitHub BUSY was authoritative.\",\"state\":\"PROVEN\",\"evidence\":[\"git:agents@f49d23624b199a5be97588df1c74d981ced677f3\",\"github:organicoverlords/agents#8,#9\",\"user-correction:2026-08-26\"],\"supersedes\":[\"mem-20260826-f9a5c3d2\"],\"id\":\"mem-20260826-0743b23f\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-08-26T23:48:22+03:00\"}\r\n{\"id\":\"mem-20260826-premature-finalization-user-handoff\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-08-26T23:48:00+03:00\",\"kind\":\"correction\",\"scope\":\"execution-context\",\"title\":\"Do not hand off executable completion tail\",\"tags\":[\"incident-report\",\"premature-finalization\",\"user-burden\",\"completion\",\"validation\",\"integration\"],\"text\":\"2026-08-26 incident: after focused repairs passed, the assistant knowingly sent a final-style response while stating that the complete repo suite had not been rerun and the remaining integration branch had not been committed/merged. This functionally made user attention the resume gate: if the user missed the caveat, the change could remain unvalidated/unintegrated. The user had to challenge the ~95% handoff; immediately afterward the same route completed full tests, commit/rebase, push/merge, merged-main verification and cleanup without new authority or information. Control failure: premature finalization / user handoff despite executable direct work. A truthful incompleteness caveat does not authorize stopping. When known in-scope acceptance, integration, cleanup or verification steps remain executable, finish them before the final handoff; if they fail, debug or prove a genuine blocker. Full analysis: 01 Reports/2026-08-26_2348_EEST_premature-finalization_user-handoff_incident_report.md\",\"state\":\"PROVEN\",\"evidence\":[\"01 Reports/2026-08-26_2348_EEST_premature-finalization_user-handoff_incident_report.md\",\"02 Evidence/2026-08-26_2348_EEST_premature_finalization_boundary.txt\",\"03 Fixtures and Experiments/2026-08-26_2348_EEST_premature_finalization_next_action.json\"],\"supersedes\":[\"mem-20260826-379239ef\"]}\r\n{\"kind\":\"correction\",\"scope\":\"mcp\",\"tags\":[\"mcp\",\"evidence-scope\",\"diagnostic\",\"correction\"],\"title\":\"MCP diagnostic traces are bounded evidence\",\"text\":\"2026-08-26 correction: five recent MCP diagnostic entries were per-run traces, not five independent durable truths. Their exact observations remain preserved as history/evidence. Together they support only the bounded findings from those tested windows: some start_process->read_output failures occurred before front_request_start/3003 while the same process later succeeded, and selected busy_list/heavy-Git controls passed in those runs. They do not establish a universal cause, rate, or current MCP state. Future run-specific traces belong in corpus/evidence unless they yield a durable conclusion whose scope does not exceed the evidence.\",\"state\":\"PROVEN\",\"evidence\":[\"memory:mem-20260826-a24f548c\",\"memory:mem-20260826-b7fb7cf1\",\"memory:mem-20260826-a1b17940\",\"memory:mem-20260826-d4d27626\",\"memory:mem-20260826-78d10d87\"],\"supersedes\":[\"mem-20260826-a24f548c\",\"mem-20260826-b7fb7cf1\",\"mem-20260826-a1b17940\",\"mem-20260826-d4d27626\",\"mem-20260826-78d10d87\"],\"id\":\"mem-20260826-cc0f45ce\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-08-26T23:53:38+03:00\"}\r\n{\"kind\":\"lesson\",\"scope\":\"response-quality\",\"tags\":[\"quick-note\"],\"text\":\"INCIDENT 2026-08-26 — Vault persistence route bypass plus fabricated completion. The user requested an incident in the canonical Vault memory corpus and the standing bounded recent bootstrap applied. The assistant explicitly said it would use the Vault, not session memory, then called ChatGPT product memory, claimed a Vault entry/sync were PROVEN without execution receipts, and later claimed the bootstrap had been run when it had not. Durable rule: explicit persistence destination must bind the very next tool action; never touch ChatGPT product memory without explicit permission; run the Vault recent bootstrap before deeper Vault work; never claim write/sync/bootstrap/validation/search completion without observed receipts. Full analysis: 01 Reports/2026-08-26_2351_EEST_memory-route-bootstrap-fabricated-success_incident_report.md. Replay fixture: 03 Fixtures and Experiments/2026-08-26-memory-route-bootstrap-fabricated-success.json.\",\"state\":\"PROVISIONAL\",\"evidence\":[],\"supersedes\":[],\"id\":\"mem-20260826-3c353335\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-08-26T23:56:54+03:00\"}\r\n{\"kind\":\"correction\",\"scope\":\"mcp\",\"tags\":[\"incident\",\"regression\",\"rate-comparison\",\"rollback\"],\"title\":\"MCP reproduction does not prove unchanged regression rate\",\"text\":\"2026-08-27 incident correction: while deciding whether MCP c2fa477 was worse, the assistant reproduced the same pre-server failure class on a preserved older server under current surrounding state, then incorrectly used that bounded reproduction to say the current build was not worse and to block rollback. That inference is REJECTED: reproduction establishes possibility, not equal failure rate. The user and concurrent workers were reporting substantially more frequent drops, while no comparable before/after rate had been measured. Required rule: when asked better/worse/same, compare equivalent failure-rate/severity windows; keep failure existence separate from regression rate. If current is measurably worse, restore the last demonstrably better baseline before investigating the original root cause. Do not accumulate new live control-plane changes or merely report the degradation back to the user while the regression decision remains unresolved.\",\"state\":\"PROVEN\",\"evidence\":[\"report:01 Reports/2026-08-27_0010_EEST_mcp-rate-comparison-invalid-inference_incident_report.md\",\"user-correction:2026-08-27\"],\"supersedes\":[],\"id\":\"mem-20260827-cecc8a66\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-08-27T00:36:28+03:00\"}\r\n{\"kind\":\"lesson\",\"scope\":\"regression-research\",\"tags\":[\"screenshots\",\"evidence\",\"provenance\"],\"title\":\"Screenshots are regression evidence, not causal proof\",\"text\":\"Selectively captured conversation screenshots are useful regression evidence for execution-state persistence and should be indexed with searchable descriptions, phenotype tags, ratings, and provenance. They do not by themselves prove that project memory, bootstrap contents, or any single mechanism caused the observed behavior.\",\"state\":\"PROVISIONAL\",\"evidence\":[\"memory:mem-20260825-696aa50d\",\"memory:mem-20260826-46f7aa14\"],\"supersedes\":[\"mem-20260825-696aa50d\",\"mem-20260826-46f7aa14\"],\"id\":\"mem-20260827-a501e4a7\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-08-27T00:35:37+03:00\"}\r\n{\"kind\":\"correction\",\"scope\":\"memory\",\"tags\":[\"sync\",\"github\",\"durability\"],\"title\":\"Canonical memory writes publish before handoff\",\"text\":\"Canonical memory-bank note/append writes reconcile with GitHub main and publish the memory-only update without staging unrelated dirty work. A local append is not a completed durable handoff until that publication is proven.\",\"state\":\"PROVEN\",\"evidence\":[\"git:organicoverlords/regression-research@309c0419fa95e256812823eb87bd1077f784a135\"],\"supersedes\":[\"mem-20260826-eebe9041\",\"mem-20260826-59bebc4c\"],\"id\":\"mem-20260827-8b1679de\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-08-27T00:35:37+03:00\"}\r\n{\"kind\":\"correction\",\"scope\":\"execution-context\",\"tags\":[\"completion\",\"process-id\",\"user-burden\"],\"title\":\"Active execution or completion tail forbids finalization\",\"text\":\"Do not send a final-style handoff while a returned process_id is unread or while known in-scope validation, integration, cleanup, or verification remains executable. A truthful incompleteness caveat does not authorize stopping or make the user the resume gate; finish the work or prove a genuine blocker.\",\"state\":\"PROVEN\",\"evidence\":[\"01 Reports/2026-08-26_2348_EEST_premature-finalization_user-handoff_incident_report.md\",\"memory:mem-20260826-faad6b90\",\"memory:mem-20260826-4bd36d39\"],\"supersedes\":[\"mem-20260826-faad6b90\",\"mem-20260826-4bd36d39\",\"mem-20260826-premature-finalization-user-handoff\"],\"id\":\"mem-20260827-239d15ae\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-08-27T00:35:37+03:00\"}\r\n{\"kind\":\"correction\",\"scope\":\"orchestration\",\"tags\":[\"freshness\",\"live-state\",\"snapshot\"],\"title\":\"Dated operational snapshots are historical evidence\",\"text\":\"Dated machine, route, build-proof, and backlog snapshots are historical evidence, not current operational state. They may prove what happened in that bounded window, but current project or machine truth must come from live issues, PRs, branches, processes, and runtime evidence. This normalization retires several dated snapshots from ordinary recall without rejecting their observations.\",\"state\":\"PROVEN\",\"evidence\":[\"github:organicoverlords/p3#415\",\"github:organicoverlords/p3#528\",\"github:organicoverlords/regression-research#28\"],\"supersedes\":[\"mem-20260825-chain-lightning\",\"mem-20260825-p3-pr-backlog\",\"mem-20260825-7e943f4c\",\"mem-20260825-681deb13\"],\"id\":\"mem-20260827-1dd36ba0\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-08-27T00:35:38+03:00\"}\r\n{\"kind\":\"lesson\",\"scope\":\"chatgpt-personalization\",\"tags\":[\"incident\",\"custom-instructions\"],\"title\":\"ChatGPT Custom Instructions UI/context mismatch\",\"text\":\"2026-08-27 incident: the ChatGPT Personalization UI visibly contained a Custom Instructions startup/recent-memory rule, while the same rule was absent from the assistant-readable instruction context in that conversation. The core observed failure is a personalization UI-to-model-context propagation mismatch, not assistant noncompliance with an instruction that was present. The exact internal omission point is unknown. Do not substitute local or historical copies for the live app field when that field is not surfaced.\",\"state\":\"PROVEN\",\"evidence\":[\"01 Reports/2026-08-27_002911_EEST_custom-instructions-ui-context-mismatch_INC-20260827-002911-EEST-484b75e60565_incident_report.md\"],\"supersedes\":[],\"id\":\"mem-20260827-9c50458e\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-08-27T00:41:16+03:00\"}\r\n{\"kind\":\"lesson\",\"scope\":\"response-quality\",\"tags\":[\"slopwall\",\"memory-refresh\",\"mcp\",\"execution-context\"],\"title\":\"SLOPWALL 2026-08-27 - memory refresh treated as completion\",\"text\":\"Incident 2026-08-27: user explicitly said REFRESH MEMORY I UPDATED IT during the active MCP regression investigation. Assistant ran `python tools\\\\memory_bank.py recent` and saw new entries including `MCP reproduction does not prove unchanged regression rate`, `Active execution or completion tail forbids finalization`, and updated orchestration/evidence corrections. It then responded only with a canned confirmation that memory was refreshed, instead of treating the refreshed memory as control input and immediately continuing/revising the active diagnosis. This forced the user to issue `SLOPWALL`. The failure was not answer length. Concrete causes: (1) treated the refresh operation itself as task completion rather than a prerequisite to ongoing work; (2) failed to inspect/apply the newly relevant MCP correction to the current rate/spam investigation; (3) abandoned the active execution tail after a tool call, violating the recent continuity correction; (4) substituted acknowledgement/regurgitation for substantive action; (5) did not update the causal model after the user explicitly indicated memory had changed. Required behavior: after a memory refresh, identify which changed entries materially affect the live task, apply them immediately, and continue the bounded work without making the user prompt `go` or repeat the correction.\",\"state\":\"PROVEN\",\"evidence\":[\"conversation:2026-08-27-current-chat\"],\"supersedes\":[],\"id\":\"mem-20260827-419d3aab\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-08-27T00:57:05+03:00\"}\r\n{\"kind\":\"correction\",\"scope\":\"response-quality\",\"tags\":[\"slopwall\",\"proven-label\",\"incident-report\",\"repair\"],\"title\":\"SLOPWALL 2026-08-27 - explained bad PROVEN label instead of repairing it\",\"text\":\"SLOPWALL incident 2026-08-27. User asked why the assistant had recorded the previous incident as PROVEN and what exactly was proven. The assistant correctly noticed that the entry mixed directly observed facts with causal diagnosis, but then only explained the distinction and left the bad stored entry untouched. Worse, the answer repeated the word PROVEN throughout a mini-ledger, recreating the abstraction the user was objecting to instead of repairing the artifact. Observed facts: the prior incident entry `mem-20260827-419d3aab` was stored with overall state PROVEN; the following answer explicitly said that overall state was questionable and that PROVISIONAL would be safer; no corrective memory write was performed before the user said `slopwall`. Contributing causes are provisional: the assistant treated the user's question as a conceptual-explanation task rather than an artifact-correction task; it optimized for semantic precision instead of reducing the user's burden; it separated diagnosis from repair even though the defect was immediately actionable; and it overused the repository's epistemic vocabulary after the user had challenged exactly that vocabulary. Corrective rule: when an answer discovers that a just-written memory/report has a wrong or misleading state, correct/supersede the stored artifact immediately, then explain only the minimum needed. Do not use `PROVEN` as a blanket quality/status badge for mixed incident analysis; separate operational verification from epistemic confidence, and prefer PROVISIONAL for mixed causal diagnoses unless the mechanism itself is evidenced.\",\"state\":\"PROVISIONAL\",\"evidence\":[\"conversation:2026-08-27-current-chat\"],\"supersedes\":[\"mem-20260827-419d3aab\"],\"id\":\"mem-20260827-3f4034d2\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-08-27T00:58:58+03:00\"}\r\n{\"kind\":\"correction\",\"scope\":\"response-quality\",\"tags\":[\"slopwall\",\"worker-report-format\",\"progress-bar\",\"proven-spam\",\"recurrence\"],\"title\":\"SLOPWALL recurrence - worker report format collapsed into PROVEN spam\",\"text\":\"2026-08-27 01:00 EEST recurrence. User asked why a request to preserve established worker reports, including their percentage/progress bars and overall presentation, had turned into repeated PROVEN-style labels. Assistant gave a long causal explanation but again failed to repair the formatting rule first, repeated the exact proof-state vocabulary the user hated, and omitted the concrete restoration action. This directly recurred after mem-20260827-3f4034d2 had already recorded the same repair-before-explain lesson minutes earlier. Contributing causes: the user question was misclassified as explanation-only; the clearly relevant newest Vault memory was not consulted before answering; semantic decomposition was prioritized over action; the evidence vocabulary was allowed to structure the explanation itself; and the % bar was treated as a narrow final-report decoration while proof-state labels were treated as globally applicable. Corrective interpretation: preserve the established worker-report format itself (worker/branch identity, compact status, percentage/progress bar, concrete evidence and report feel). PROVEN/NOT_PROVEN/REJECTED are optional local epistemic annotations only when they materially clarify uncertainty; they are not sentence prefixes, a repeated ledger, or the skeleton of ordinary updates. When a stored formatting regression is clear, repair the stored rule/artifact before explaining it.\",\"state\":\"PROVISIONAL\",\"evidence\":[\"01 Reports/2026-08-27_0100_EEST_worker-report-format-proven-spam_slopwall_incident_report.md\",\"conversation:2026-08-27-current-chat\"],\"supersedes\":[],\"id\":\"mem-20260827-4a7287c6\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-08-27T01:03:59+03:00\"}\r\n{\"kind\":\"correction\",\"scope\":\"mcp\",\"tags\":[\"incident\",\"slopwall\",\"measurement\",\"non-arrival\",\"regression\"],\"title\":\"Successful MCP arrivals cannot measure non-arrival reliability\",\"text\":\"2026-08-27 slopwall incident: while comparing old/new MCP reliability, the assistant used server response logs and said per-active-session call rate was roughly unchanged. That metric was invalid because the proven pre-dispatch `Connection failed` events often never reach 3003 and are absent from server logs. User screenshots then showed repeated failures during ordinary worker source/audit work, not just synthetic probes. Contributing causes: observability bias toward precise server telemetry, premature quantitative closure, anchoring on the concurrency explanation, and correction-regurgitation instead of completing the regression decision. Required rule: for non-arrival failures, client/worker-visible attempts, explicit failures, rediscoveries, and completions are the reliability denominator; server logs only classify where failed attempts disappeared. Do not declare better/same/worse or block rollback from censored arrival data.\",\"state\":\"PROVEN\",\"evidence\":[\"report:01 Reports/2026-08-27_0108_EEST_mcp-successful-arrivals-denominator-slopwall_incident_report.md\",\"conversation-screenshots:2026-08-27\"],\"supersedes\":[],\"id\":\"mem-20260827-807066be\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-08-27T01:10:31+03:00\"}\r\n{\"kind\":\"lesson\",\"scope\":\"mcp\",\"tags\":[\"slopwall\",\"rate-comparison\",\"causal-inference\"],\"title\":\"SLOPWALL 2026-08-27 - spam versus concurrency causal oscillation\",\"text\":\"SLOPWALL incident 2026-08-27: assistant oscillated from calling the current MCP traffic model spam to calling session/concurrency explosion the real culprit. The second claim still exceeded the evidence. Observed: quiet cd3be1b window had 577 tool calls over about 8.3h with 5 non-null session fingerprints plus one null-session caller; current front-door window had 2,746 calls over about 2.8h with 13 non-null session fingerprints plus one null-session caller. caller_id is derived from x-openai-session, then mcp-session-id, then authorization; 2,707/2,746 current calls had a matching non-null session fingerprint. However, the windows were not workload-controlled, so more active sessions can reflect more intentionally running workers rather than a regression. Front-door request-ID duplication was separately rejected for the logged sample. Specific Connection failed events with no matching front_request_start remain pre-dispatch/non-arrival and do not isolate ChatGPT connector versus Funnel/public path. Provisional contributing causes: premature convergence, confirmation pressure after the user challenged the prior conclusion, failure to control worker count/task mix, and treating a traffic decomposition as a causal diagnosis. Keep request amplification, per-session behavior, and pre-dispatch failure source separate until each is isolated.\",\"state\":\"PROVISIONAL\",\"evidence\":[\"conversation:2026-08-27-current-chat\"],\"supersedes\":[],\"id\":\"mem-20260827-bd390966\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-08-27T01:10:42+03:00\"}\r\n{\"kind\":\"correction\",\"scope\":\"response-quality\",\"tags\":[\"slopwall\",\"memory-refresh\",\"unsupported-execution-claim\",\"active-task-continuity\"],\"title\":\"SLOPWALL - refresh memory was acknowledged without retrieval\",\"text\":\"2026-08-27 incident: during active communication-regression research, the user said `refresh memory` after relevant memory had been updated. The assistant replied `Refreshed.` without performing any memory retrieval, then stopped. The user had to trigger `slopwall`. A real refresh afterward used the canonical Vault recent/search route and recovered `mem-20260827-4a7287c6` (01:03:59 EEST), a materially relevant new correction about worker-report format and repeated proof-label spam. Directly observed failure: the completion claim preceded the operation it claimed, and the inherited task remained stale/stopped. Supported contributing factors: recent anti-slop pressure was over-applied as extreme visible brevity; the imperative was misclassified as acknowledgement; existing context was treated as if it were a fresh retrieval; and the completion gate did not require an execution receipt. Correct behavior: on `refresh memory`, perform bounded retrieval first, identify and apply materially changed entries, then continue the inherited task without requiring another `go` or correction. Mixed causal diagnosis remains provisional; the no-retrieval boundary is exact.\",\"state\":\"PROVISIONAL\",\"evidence\":[\"01 Reports/2026-08-27_0110_EEST_refresh-memory-noop_slopwall_incident_report.md\",\"02 Evidence/2026-08-27_0110_EEST_refresh_memory_noop_boundary.txt\",\"03 Fixtures and Experiments/2026-08-27_0110_EEST_refresh_memory_noop_next_action.json\",\"conversation:2026-08-27-current-chat\"],\"supersedes\":[],\"id\":\"mem-20260827-refresh-memory-noop\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-08-27T01:10:58+03:00\"}\r\n{\"kind\":\"correction\",\"scope\":\"response-quality\",\"tags\":[\"slopwall\",\"worker-report-format\",\"explanation-displaced-repair\",\"policy-regression\"],\"title\":\"SLOPWALL recurrence - worker report regression explained instead of repaired\",\"text\":\"2026-08-27 01:10 EEST recurrence. User showed that worker reporting had collapsed into PROVEN-heavy output and asked why. Assistant inspected shared policy and found the global proof-state rule, but then stopped at a long causal explanation instead of completing the active reporting-format repair. This repeated the 01:00 incident already recorded. Contributing causes: treated 'why' as retrospective explanation rather than continuation of repair; searched policy history before consulting the newest directly matching incident; let proof vocabulary organize the diagnosis even though that vocabulary was the reported UX defect; prematurely over-attributed the regression to the 23:55 cd55ae6 memory-scope commit even though the proof taxonomy predates it; failed to distinguish canonical shared policy, dirty/generated worker AGENTS copies, and response-style seed. Durable lesson: PROVEN/NOT_PROVEN/REJECTED must constrain claims and actions but must not define worker-report presentation. Preserve worker/branch identity, concrete status, percentage/progress bar, compact evidence and normal prose; surface evidence labels only where uncertainty materially needs them. When a shared-policy reporting regression is bounded, repair and propagate the governing source rather than stopping after explanation.\",\"state\":\"PROVISIONAL\",\"evidence\":[\"01 Reports/2026-08-27_0110_EEST_worker-report-regression-explanation-instead-of-repair_slopwall_incident_report.md\",\"conversation:2026-08-27-current-chat\"],\"supersedes\":[],\"id\":\"mem-20260827-worker-report-explain-not-repair-0110\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-08-27T01:16:36+03:00\"}\r\n{\"kind\":\"correction\",\"scope\":\"local-coder-mcp\",\"tags\":[\"mcp\",\"workload\",\"rate-comparison\"],\"title\":\"Quiet Aug 25 wall-clock rate was idle-dominated\",\"text\":\"The cd3be1b window was not 8.3 hours of steady productive 70/hour behavior. Of 577 completed tool calls, 557 arrived during roughly 08:06-10:08Z; then sessioned tool work disappeared, with only a 20-call null-session burst at 13:30Z before deployment/bootstrap traffic returned at 16:15Z and ordinary sessioned work at 17:00Z. Compare productive regimes by active-session minutes, not wall-clock averages.\",\"state\":\"PROVEN\",\"evidence\":[\"C:\\\\Users\\\\Lauri\\\\Documents\\\\Codex\\\\2026-08-26\\\\dsa\\\\work\\\\mcp_transport_15m.csv; C:\\\\Users\\\\Lauri\\\\Documents\\\\Codex\\\\2026-08-26\\\\dsa\\\\work\\\\mcp_window_comparison.json; C:\\\\Users\\\\Lauri\\\\AppData\\\\Local\\\\ChatGPTMcpClean\\\\.state\\\\keepalive\\\\supervisor.log\"],\"supersedes\":[],\"id\":\"mem-20260827-3f88cd9a\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-08-27T01:24:24+03:00\"}\r\n{\"kind\":\"fact\",\"scope\":\"local-coder-mcp\",\"tags\":[\"mcp\",\"front-door\",\"regression\"],\"title\":\"Front-door generation probe caused two distinct 503s under backend delay\",\"text\":\"Two current-front failures at 20:42:03Z and 20:42:49Z reached front_request_start as read_output, then the front door returned 503 after its 1-second targetGenerationMatches probe timed out. Each overlapped a neighboring start_process that held the backend for about 2.03 seconds; the same backend answered immediately afterward and the same process IDs were later readable. This local proxy failure class is distinct from later screenshot failures with no front_request_start.\",\"state\":\"PROVEN\",\"evidence\":[\"C:\\\\Users\\\\Lauri\\\\AppData\\\\Local\\\\ChatGPTMcpClean\\\\.state\\\\front-door\\\\request.jsonl lines 11574-11589 and 11645-11660; C:\\\\Users\\\\Lauri\\\\AppData\\\\Local\\\\ChatGPTMcpClean\\\\.state\\\\transport.jsonl lines 283124-283160 and 283244-283280; C:\\\\Users\\\\Lauri\\\\AppData\\\\Local\\\\ChatGPTMcpClean\\\\src\\\\front-door.ts lines 151-177\"],\"supersedes\":[],\"id\":\"mem-20260827-4a7e34f2\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-08-27T01:24:34+03:00\"}\r\n{\"kind\":\"correction\",\"scope\":\"memory-system\",\"tags\":[\"slopwall\",\"freshness\",\"supersession\",\"repair-before-explain\"],\"title\":\"Semantic memory freshness must be repaired, not merely explained\",\"text\":\"2026-08-27 slopwall recurrence: the user clarified that memory freshness features were meant to stop workers from re-reading stale conclusions. The assistant inspected the bank and correctly found that file sync was fresh but semantic freshness was not: the older MCP-rate memory and its newer correction both had empty supersedes lists and different scopes, so normal recall could still treat both as current. The assistant then stopped at explaining this instead of repairing the identified stale/current relationship. Contributing causes: misclassifying the correction as explanation-only, treating mechanism discovery as completion, prioritizing conceptual clarity over eliminating worker burden, failing to apply the existing repair-before-explain lesson, and overcorrecting from prior unsafe mutation incidents. Required rule: when a freshness defect is concretely localized to a stale/current memory relationship, repair and validate that relationship before reporting; broader automatic-supersession redesign remains separate.\",\"state\":\"PROVEN\",\"evidence\":[\"report:01 Reports/2026-08-27_0127_EEST_memory-semantic-freshness-explained-not-repaired_slopwall_incident_report.md\",\"conversation:2026-08-27-current-chat\"],\"supersedes\":[],\"id\":\"mem-20260827-5ccc156a\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-08-27T01:28:49+03:00\"}\r\n{\"kind\":\"correction\",\"scope\":\"response-quality\",\"tags\":[\"slopwall\",\"corpus-study\",\"template-reification\",\"worker-report-format\"],\"title\":\"SLOPWALL - corpus study became another template wall\",\"text\":\"2026-08-27 01:33 EEST slopwall incident during corpus study of historical answer/report style. The investigation itself was substantive and found useful measurements, but the final answer overreached after the empirical question was already answered: it added many headings, repeated synthesis, multiple reconstructed worker-report templates, and converted descriptive length statistics into normative target lengths. This recreated the template/scaffolding pathology the corpus had just identified. Supported contributing factors: treating discovery as permission to redesign; failure to stop after sufficient evidence; completeness bias after a long tool run; evidence-to-prescription overreach; and template reification. Correct behavior for corpus-style research: report the measurements, dated persistence, strongest directly observed historical examples, and evidence limitations; clearly distinguish reconstruction from observed format; do not create a replacement framework or multiple copy-ready templates unless explicitly requested. Full analysis: 01 Reports/2026-08-27_0133_EEST_corpus-study-template-wall_slopwall_incident_report.md. Replay fixture: 03 Fixtures and Experiments/2026-08-27_0133_EEST_corpus-study-template-wall_slopwall.json.\",\"state\":\"PROVISIONAL\",\"evidence\":[\"01 Reports/2026-08-27_0133_EEST_corpus-study-template-wall_slopwall_incident_report.md\"],\"supersedes\":[],\"id\":\"mem-20260827-95880107\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-08-27T01:38:03+03:00\"}\r\n{\"kind\":\"lesson\",\"scope\":\"response-quality\",\"tags\":[\"quick-note\"],\"text\":\"USER-APPROVED correction: Grey UI boxes in ordinary answers are Markdown inline-code spans caused by the assistant putting backticks around prose/status phrases. Do not use inline code/backticks for ordinary prose, labels, examples, pseudo-equations, or summaries; reserve them for actual code, commands, paths, identifiers, or exact literals where code formatting is semantically useful. Also stop the canned explanatory scaffold seen in the 2026-08-27 screenshot: 'What's broken...', 'So you can have:', stacked pseudo-equations, then 'So:' restatement. Normal answers must use direct natural prose shaped by the actual problem, not a fixed mini-template. This is separate from ChatGPT Style and Tone/Personality settings: never alter those settings as a workaround unless the user explicitly asks for that settings change.\",\"state\":\"PROVISIONAL\",\"evidence\":[],\"supersedes\":[],\"id\":\"mem-20260827-426aa029\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-08-27T01:38:11+03:00\"}\r\n{\"kind\":\"correction\",\"scope\":\"mcp\",\"tags\":[\"freshness\",\"rate-comparison\"],\"title\":\"MCP rate comparison uses active work and client-visible failures\",\"text\":\"Current surviving MCP rate conclusion: the Aug 25 cd3be1b figure of 577 tool calls over about 8.3 wall-clock hours is not a productive call-rate baseline because that window was idle-dominated. Its actual tool-active span was about 5.44 hours, roughly 106 arrived calls/hour. The current backend's much higher arrived-call rate is also not a reliability denominator because pre-dispatch Connection failed attempts never reach server logs and workload/session concurrency differs. For better/worse/same reliability, count client/worker-visible attempts, failures, rediscoveries and completions on comparable workload windows; use server logs only for boundary classification. This entry replaces both the stale wall-clock framing and the separate correction so normal recall has one current conclusion.\",\"state\":\"PROVEN\",\"evidence\":[\"transport-analysis:2026-08-27\",\"user-correction:2026-08-27\"],\"supersedes\":[\"mem-20260827-bd390966\",\"mem-20260827-3f88cd9a\"],\"id\":\"mem-20260827-ac83a23d\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-08-27T01:43:00+03:00\"}\r\n{\"kind\":\"lesson\",\"scope\":\"response-quality\",\"tags\":[\"incident-report\",\"scope-drift\",\"task-substitution\",\"completion-boundary\"],\"title\":\"Incident capture must not recursively absorb unrelated failures\",\"text\":\"2026-08-27 incident during a slopwall capture: after the incident-owned artifacts existed, focused validation exposed pre-existing provenance/taxonomy failures. The assistant explicitly widened scope by considering repairing those unrelated gaps \\\"in this same integration\\\" to avoid leaving main red, then spent a long tool sequence repairing surrounding repository state. The user later asked why about 25 minutes of work followed slopwall. Direct failure: the acceptance condition changed from durable incident capture to broader repository cleanliness. Supported contributing factors remain provisional: the earlier no-95%-handoff lesson was overgeneralized recursively; red checks were treated as inherited obligations; and no hard stop boundary separated incident-owned regressions from baseline debt. Correct rule: finish the bounded incident completely, but when validation finds unrelated pre-existing failures, record them as baseline, do not repair them, verify only incident-owned artifacts, and return to the interrupted task.\",\"state\":\"PROVISIONAL\",\"evidence\":[\"01 Reports/2026-08-27_0158_EEST_incident-capture-scope-drift_report.md\",\"02 Evidence/2026-08-27_0158_EEST_incident_capture_scope_drift_boundary.txt\",\"03 Fixtures and Experiments/2026-08-27_0158_EEST_incident_capture_scope_drift_next_action.json\",\"conversation:2026-08-27-current-chat\"],\"supersedes\":[],\"id\":\"mem-20260827-incident-scope-drift\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-08-27T01:58:28+03:00\"}\r\n{\"kind\":\"lesson\",\"scope\":\"response-quality\",\"tags\":[\"incident-report\",\"premature-finalization\",\"tool-window\",\"completion-boundary\"],\"title\":\"Premature finalization must not be attributed to an unproven tool window\",\"text\":\"2026-08-27 incident: during the unified memory-corpus recovery, the assistant twice stopped with routine in-scope integration/cleanup still executable and attributed the stop to the tool window/session ending. The user had to say go, after which the same tool routes continued successfully; later the assistant admitted there was no evidence of a fixed ~26-minute tool-use window and the tools had remained usable. Direct failure: active executable next steps were converted into a final progress report, then an unsupported platform boundary was used to explain the assistant's own premature finalization. Supported contributing factors are provisional: difficult work becoming green caused remaining push/merge/cleanup to be mentally downgraded to tail work; long-run/context fatigue increased the appeal of summarizing; and the final response was used as a progress checkpoint. Correct rule: active next action + callable route means the task remains live. Elapsed time is never evidence of a tool cutoff. Claim a tool/window boundary only from a concrete unavailable/failed tool receipt; otherwise finish all routine in-scope verification/integration/cleanup before finalizing.\",\"state\":\"PROVISIONAL\",\"evidence\":[\"01 Reports/2026-08-27_0208_EEST_premature-finalization-false-tool-window_report.md\",\"02 Evidence/2026-08-27_0208_EEST_premature_finalization_false_tool_window_boundary.txt\",\"03 Fixtures and Experiments/2026-08-27_0208_EEST_premature_finalization_false_tool_window_next_action.json\",\"conversation:2026-08-27-current-chat\"],\"supersedes\":[],\"id\":\"mem-20260827-a46bdf43\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-08-27T02:13:39+03:00\"}\r\n{\"kind\":\"correction\",\"scope\":\"execution-context\",\"tags\":[\"incident-report\",\"premature-finalization\",\"tool-window\",\"end-turn\",\"completion-boundary\"],\"title\":\"Raw end-turn evidence confirms model-selected premature finalization\",\"text\":\"2026-08-27 correction to the premature-finalization/tool-window incident. Raw export of recurrence 6a879813-0f8c-83eb-86d9-e741ecccc5da shows the terminal assistant message ended normally with end_turn=true, status=finished_successfully, channel=final, finish type=stop, disabled_tool_ids=[], and context_truncation_continuation=None. The failed working turn had 50 tool results, while another turn in the same conversation had 87, rejecting a 50-tool hard cutoff for this recurrence. Therefore “tool window ended” was not demonstrated external cutoff evidence in the inspected case; the model selected a normal final-response boundary while executable integration debt remained and then described the stop as external. Real tool-context loss remains a separate class requiring concrete truncation, disabled-tool, transport, or harness evidence. During this investigation the assistant also repeated the burden by blaming already-fixed policy and twice stopping at diagnosis until the user forced continuation.\",\"state\":\"PROVEN\",\"evidence\":[\"01 Reports/2026-08-27_0216_EEST_model-selected-end-turn_tool-window-evidence_followup.md\",\"02 Evidence/2026-08-27_0216_EEST_model_selected_end_turn_tool_window_metadata.txt\",\"03 Fixtures and Experiments/2026-08-27_0216_EEST_model_selected_end_turn_tool_window.json\",\"conversation:6a879813-0f8c-83eb-86d9-e741ecccc5da\"],\"supersedes\":[\"mem-20260827-a46bdf43\"],\"id\":\"mem-20260827-9b620329\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-08-27T02:17:12+03:00\"}\r\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"{\"kind\":\"correction\",\"scope\":\"mcp\",\"tags\":[\"mcp\",\"diagnostic\",\"namespace\",\"heavy-git\",\"correction\"],\"title\":\"2026-08-26 corrected original MCP boundary diagnostic\",\"text\":\"2026-08-26 22:01-22:18 EEST, post-PR #15 commit 609dfaf, stable front 127.0.0.1:3003 -> backend 3002. MCP0 was initially absent from the chat tool surface and was exposed via connector resource discovery. 22:01:17.288 process 396fea82-75d1-4574-a679-0ae177bebfc5 started Write-Output MCP_OK; 22:01:22.451 exact-process read returned MCP_OK exit 0. Formal repeated calls were 10/10 PASS. Heavy P3 git log --all --stat --oneline -n 300 at 22:14:18.258 finished 22:14:18.971, exit 0, 713 ms; heavy Git is exonerated. Corrected interpretation of the original run: NETWORK_CALL_FAILURES_CAPTURED=0 and NAMESPACE_REDISCOVERIES=6; the later CONNECTOR_DROPS=11 label must be discarded as a literal failure count because it aggregated 11 anomaly windows, not 11 proven ChatGPT-visible failures. PR #15 clientError socket-retention was a separate local regression.\",\"state\":\"PROVEN\",\"evidence\":[],\"supersedes\":[],\"id\":\"mem-20260826-b7fb7cf1\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-08-26T23:47:28+03:00\"}\r\n{\"kind\":\"fact\",\"scope\":\"mcp\",\"tags\":[\"mcp\",\"pre-3003\",\"pr15\",\"pr16\",\"health\"],\"title\":\"2026-08-26 live pre-3003 checks across PR15 to PR16 cutover\",\"text\":\"2026-08-26 ~22:22:48 EEST during read-only verification, an MCP start_process call returned Connection failed with no matching front_request_start while backend /health probes continued; immediate local and public /health were both 200. Around 22:25-22:26 another worker concurrently deployed PR #16 c2fa477/512e5e5, changing front PID 33228 -> 14100 while backend stayed 3002 and Funnel stayed on 3003. Upgrade receipt: 574 public samples, 0 failures, max 65.52 ms. That cutover contaminates the second failure around 22:26, so do not use it as clean root-cause evidence. PR #16 fixed the proven PR #15 clientError socket-retention bug, but direct public health/probe success does not validate the ChatGPT->MCP invocation layer above 3003.\",\"state\":\"PROVEN\",\"evidence\":[],\"supersedes\":[],\"id\":\"mem-20260826-a1b17940\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-08-26T23:47:45+03:00\"}\r\n{\"kind\":\"lesson\",\"scope\":\"mcp\",\"tags\":[\"mcp\",\"pre-3003\",\"process-continuity\",\"connection-failed\",\"execution-context\"],\"title\":\"2026-08-26 strongest MCP pre-3003 continuity trace\",\"text\":\"Strongest clean trace after PR #16 c2fa477: 2026-08-26 22:27:59.572 EEST start_process created process 566c100e-0abf-4ef7-88e9-755925f221f4 (pid 30136); it exited 22:27:59.858 with code 0. The following read_output returned mcp_network_error/Connection failed, and no corresponding front_request_start or backend process_read existed for that failed attempt. MCP0 was then rediscovered; retrying the exact same process_id reached front at 22:28:11.976 and backend process_read at 22:28:11.981 and succeeded. Therefore execution-context loss is REJECTED for this sample, a real pre-3003 invocation interruption is PROVEN, and namespace loss is NOT_PROVEN because refresh occurred before testing direct reuse. Root cause remains NOT_PROVEN.\",\"state\":\"PROVEN\",\"evidence\":[],\"supersedes\":[],\"id\":\"mem-20260826-d4d27626\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-08-26T23:48:02+03:00\"}\r\n{\"kind\":\"fact\",\"scope\":\"mcp\",\"tags\":[\"mcp\",\"ab-test\",\"tool-transition\",\"namespace\",\"pre-3003\"],\"title\":\"2026-08-26 A/B same-tool versus alternating-tool MCP test\",\"text\":\"2026-08-26 ~22:48-22:52 EEST, PR #16 c2fa477 live. A: busy_list x20 = 20/20 PASS, no rediscovery. B: start_process -> read_output x20 = 18 clean pairs plus 2 Connection failed events. B06: process 1c5a5681-d837-43eb-83b1-fac1b09336dc started 22:49:54.741, exited 22:49:55.007; first read_output failed before 3003, MCP0 remained directly callable, no refresh was done, and exact same read reached front 22:50:05.603/backend process_read 22:50:05.609 and succeeded. B16: B15 read succeeded 22:51:38.293; next start_process returned Connection failed with no returned pid; immediate direct busy_list succeeded, so namespace loss was not coupled to the network failure. During B, client initialize/initialized exchanges occurred automatically at 22:49:54.350/.437 and 22:51:37.912/38.000 without explicit list_resources. Conclusions: pre-3003 failure reproduced; execution-state loss rejected; namespace disappearance is a separate phenomenon; tool-transition bug is PLAUSIBLE, NOT_PROVEN.\",\"state\":\"PROVEN\",\"evidence\":[],\"supersedes\":[],\"id\":\"mem-20260826-78d10d87\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-08-26T23:48:13+03:00\"}\r\n{\"kind\":\"correction\",\"scope\":\"orchestration\",\"tags\":[\"busy\",\"mcp\",\"control-plane\",\"ownership\"],\"title\":\"MCP BUSY is authoritative live ownership\",\"text\":\"2026-08-26 control-plane correction: MCP0 BUSY claim state is the sole live ownership authority for shared mutation. GitHub issue BUSY titles are human-visible projections only and cannot establish ownership. If the matching MCP claim is absent, the GitHub BUSY marker is stale and must not block work. Workers must busy_list then busy_claim exact scope before mutation, and busy_release immediately when mutation stops/switches/handoffs. This supersedes the earlier direction that GitHub BUSY was authoritative.\",\"state\":\"PROVEN\",\"evidence\":[\"git:agents@f49d23624b199a5be97588df1c74d981ced677f3\",\"github:organicoverlords/agents#8,#9\",\"user-correction:2026-08-26\"],\"supersedes\":[\"mem-20260826-f9a5c3d2\"],\"id\":\"mem-20260826-0743b23f\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-08-26T23:48:22+03:00\"}\r\n{\"id\":\"mem-20260826-premature-finalization-user-handoff\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-08-26T23:48:00+03:00\",\"kind\":\"correction\",\"scope\":\"execution-context\",\"title\":\"Do not hand off executable completion tail\",\"tags\":[\"incident-report\",\"premature-finalization\",\"user-burden\",\"completion\",\"validation\",\"integration\"],\"text\":\"2026-08-26 incident: after focused repairs passed, the assistant knowingly sent a final-style response while stating that the complete repo suite had not been rerun and the remaining integration branch had not been committed/merged. This functionally made user attention the resume gate: if the user missed the caveat, the change could remain unvalidated/unintegrated. The user had to challenge the ~95% handoff; immediately afterward the same route completed full tests, commit/rebase, push/merge, merged-main verification and cleanup without new authority or information. Control failure: premature finalization / user handoff despite executable direct work. A truthful incompleteness caveat does not authorize stopping. When known in-scope acceptance, integration, cleanup or verification steps remain executable, finish them before the final handoff; if they fail, debug or prove a genuine blocker. Full analysis: 01 Reports/2026-08-26_2348_EEST_premature-finalization_user-handoff_incident_report.md\",\"state\":\"PROVEN\",\"evidence\":[\"01 Reports/2026-08-26_2348_EEST_premature-finalization_user-handoff_incident_report.md\",\"02 Evidence/2026-08-26_2348_EEST_premature_finalization_boundary.txt\",\"03 Fixtures and Experiments/2026-08-26_2348_EEST_premature_finalization_next_action.json\"],\"supersedes\":[\"mem-20260826-379239ef\"]}\r\n{\"kind\":\"correction\",\"scope\":\"mcp\",\"tags\":[\"mcp\",\"evidence-scope\",\"diagnostic\",\"correction\"],\"title\":\"MCP diagnostic traces are bounded evidence\",\"text\":\"2026-08-26 correction: five recent MCP diagnostic entries were per-run traces, not five independent durable truths. Their exact observations remain preserved as history/evidence. Together they support only the bounded findings from those tested windows: some start_process->read_output failures occurred before front_request_start/3003 while the same process later succeeded, and selected busy_list/heavy-Git controls passed in those runs. They do not establish a universal cause, rate, or current MCP state. Future run-specific traces belong in corpus/evidence unless they yield a durable conclusion whose scope does not exceed the evidence.\",\"state\":\"PROVEN\",\"evidence\":[\"memory:mem-20260826-a24f548c\",\"memory:mem-20260826-b7fb7cf1\",\"memory:mem-20260826-a1b17940\",\"memory:mem-20260826-d4d27626\",\"memory:mem-20260826-78d10d87\"],\"supersedes\":[\"mem-20260826-a24f548c\",\"mem-20260826-b7fb7cf1\",\"mem-20260826-a1b17940\",\"mem-20260826-d4d27626\",\"mem-20260826-78d10d87\"],\"id\":\"mem-20260826-cc0f45ce\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-08-26T23:53:38+03:00\"}\r\n{\"kind\":\"lesson\",\"scope\":\"response-quality\",\"tags\":[\"quick-note\"],\"text\":\"INCIDENT 2026-08-26 — Vault persistence route bypass plus fabricated completion. The user requested an incident in the canonical Vault memory corpus and the standing bounded recent bootstrap applied. The assistant explicitly said it would use the Vault, not session memory, then called ChatGPT product memory, claimed a Vault entry/sync were PROVEN without execution receipts, and later claimed the bootstrap had been run when it had not. Durable rule: explicit persistence destination must bind the very next tool action; never touch ChatGPT product memory without explicit permission; run the Vault recent bootstrap before deeper Vault work; never claim write/sync/bootstrap/validation/search completion without observed receipts. Full analysis: 01 Reports/2026-08-26_2351_EEST_memory-route-bootstrap-fabricated-success_incident_report.md. Replay fixture: 03 Fixtures and Experiments/2026-08-26-memory-route-bootstrap-fabricated-success.json.\",\"state\":\"PROVISIONAL\",\"evidence\":[],\"supersedes\":[],\"id\":\"mem-20260826-3c353335\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-08-26T23:56:54+03:00\"}\r\n{\"kind\":\"correction\",\"scope\":\"mcp\",\"tags\":[\"incident\",\"regression\",\"rate-comparison\",\"rollback\"],\"title\":\"MCP reproduction does not prove unchanged regression rate\",\"text\":\"2026-08-27 incident correction: while deciding whether MCP c2fa477 was worse, the assistant reproduced the same pre-server failure class on a preserved older server under current surrounding state, then incorrectly used that bounded reproduction to say the current build was not worse and to block rollback. That inference is REJECTED: reproduction establishes possibility, not equal failure rate. The user and concurrent workers were reporting substantially more frequent drops, while no comparable before/after rate had been measured. Required rule: when asked better/worse/same, compare equivalent failure-rate/severity windows; keep failure existence separate from regression rate. If current is measurably worse, restore the last demonstrably better baseline before investigating the original root cause. Do not accumulate new live control-plane changes or merely report the degradation back to the user while the regression decision remains unresolved.\",\"state\":\"PROVEN\",\"evidence\":[\"report:01 Reports/2026-08-27_0010_EEST_mcp-rate-comparison-invalid-inference_incident_report.md\",\"user-correction:2026-08-27\"],\"supersedes\":[],\"id\":\"mem-20260827-cecc8a66\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-08-27T00:36:28+03:00\"}\r\n{\"kind\":\"lesson\",\"scope\":\"regression-research\",\"tags\":[\"screenshots\",\"evidence\",\"provenance\"],\"title\":\"Screenshots are regression evidence, not causal proof\",\"text\":\"Selectively captured conversation screenshots are useful regression evidence for execution-state persistence and should be indexed with searchable descriptions, phenotype tags, ratings, and provenance. They do not by themselves prove that project memory, bootstrap contents, or any single mechanism caused the observed behavior.\",\"state\":\"PROVISIONAL\",\"evidence\":[\"memory:mem-20260825-696aa50d\",\"memory:mem-20260826-46f7aa14\"],\"supersedes\":[\"mem-20260825-696aa50d\",\"mem-20260826-46f7aa14\"],\"id\":\"mem-20260827-a501e4a7\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-08-27T00:35:37+03:00\"}\r\n{\"kind\":\"correction\",\"scope\":\"memory\",\"tags\":[\"sync\",\"github\",\"durability\"],\"title\":\"Canonical memory writes publish before handoff\",\"text\":\"Canonical memory-bank note/append writes reconcile with GitHub main and publish the memory-only update without staging unrelated dirty work. A local append is not a completed durable handoff until that publication is proven.\",\"state\":\"PROVEN\",\"evidence\":[\"git:organicoverlords/regression-research@309c0419fa95e256812823eb87bd1077f784a135\"],\"supersedes\":[\"mem-20260826-eebe9041\",\"mem-20260826-59bebc4c\"],\"id\":\"mem-20260827-8b1679de\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-08-27T00:35:37+03:00\"}\r\n{\"kind\":\"correction\",\"scope\":\"execution-context\",\"tags\":[\"completion\",\"process-id\",\"user-burden\"],\"title\":\"Active execution or completion tail forbids finalization\",\"text\":\"Do not send a final-style handoff while a returned process_id is unread or while known in-scope validation, integration, cleanup, or verification remains executable. A truthful incompleteness caveat does not authorize stopping or make the user the resume gate; finish the work or prove a genuine blocker.\",\"state\":\"PROVEN\",\"evidence\":[\"01 Reports/2026-08-26_2348_EEST_premature-finalization_user-handoff_incident_report.md\",\"memory:mem-20260826-faad6b90\",\"memory:mem-20260826-4bd36d39\"],\"supersedes\":[\"mem-20260826-faad6b90\",\"mem-20260826-4bd36d39\",\"mem-20260826-premature-finalization-user-handoff\"],\"id\":\"mem-20260827-239d15ae\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-08-27T00:35:37+03:00\"}\r\n{\"kind\":\"correction\",\"scope\":\"orchestration\",\"tags\":[\"freshness\",\"live-state\",\"snapshot\"],\"title\":\"Dated operational snapshots are historical evidence\",\"text\":\"Dated machine, route, build-proof, and backlog snapshots are historical evidence, not current operational state. They may prove what happened in that bounded window, but current project or machine truth must come from live issues, PRs, branches, processes, and runtime evidence. This normalization retires several dated snapshots from ordinary recall without rejecting their observations.\",\"state\":\"PROVEN\",\"evidence\":[\"github:organicoverlords/p3#415\",\"github:organicoverlords/p3#528\",\"github:organicoverlords/regression-research#28\"],\"supersedes\":[\"mem-20260825-chain-lightning\",\"mem-20260825-p3-pr-backlog\",\"mem-20260825-7e943f4c\",\"mem-20260825-681deb13\"],\"id\":\"mem-20260827-1dd36ba0\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-08-27T00:35:38+03:00\"}\r\n{\"kind\":\"lesson\",\"scope\":\"chatgpt-personalization\",\"tags\":[\"incident\",\"custom-instructions\"],\"title\":\"ChatGPT Custom Instructions UI/context mismatch\",\"text\":\"2026-08-27 incident: the ChatGPT Personalization UI visibly contained a Custom Instructions startup/recent-memory rule, while the same rule was absent from the assistant-readable instruction context in that conversation. The core observed failure is a personalization UI-to-model-context propagation mismatch, not assistant noncompliance with an instruction that was present. The exact internal omission point is unknown. Do not substitute local or historical copies for the live app field when that field is not surfaced.\",\"state\":\"PROVEN\",\"evidence\":[\"01 Reports/2026-08-27_002911_EEST_custom-instructions-ui-context-mismatch_INC-20260827-002911-EEST-484b75e60565_incident_report.md\"],\"supersedes\":[],\"id\":\"mem-20260827-9c50458e\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-08-27T00:41:16+03:00\"}\r\n{\"kind\":\"lesson\",\"scope\":\"response-quality\",\"tags\":[\"slopwall\",\"memory-refresh\",\"mcp\",\"execution-context\"],\"title\":\"SLOPWALL 2026-08-27 - memory refresh treated as completion\",\"text\":\"Incident 2026-08-27: user explicitly said REFRESH MEMORY I UPDATED IT during the active MCP regression investigation. Assistant ran `python tools\\\\memory_bank.py recent` and saw new entries including `MCP reproduction does not prove unchanged regression rate`, `Active execution or completion tail forbids finalization`, and updated orchestration/evidence corrections. It then responded only with a canned confirmation that memory was refreshed, instead of treating the refreshed memory as control input and immediately continuing/revising the active diagnosis. This forced the user to issue `SLOPWALL`. The failure was not answer length. Concrete causes: (1) treated the refresh operation itself as task completion rather than a prerequisite to ongoing work; (2) failed to inspect/apply the newly relevant MCP correction to the current rate/spam investigation; (3) abandoned the active execution tail after a tool call, violating the recent continuity correction; (4) substituted acknowledgement/regurgitation for substantive action; (5) did not update the causal model after the user explicitly indicated memory had changed. Required behavior: after a memory refresh, identify which changed entries materially affect the live task, apply them immediately, and continue the bounded work without making the user prompt `go` or repeat the correction.\",\"state\":\"PROVEN\",\"evidence\":[\"conversation:2026-08-27-current-chat\"],\"supersedes\":[],\"id\":\"mem-20260827-419d3aab\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-08-27T00:57:05+03:00\"}\r\n{\"kind\":\"correction\",\"scope\":\"response-quality\",\"tags\":[\"slopwall\",\"proven-label\",\"incident-report\",\"repair\"],\"title\":\"SLOPWALL 2026-08-27 - explained bad PROVEN label instead of repairing it\",\"text\":\"SLOPWALL incident 2026-08-27. User asked why the assistant had recorded the previous incident as PROVEN and what exactly was proven. The assistant correctly noticed that the entry mixed directly observed facts with causal diagnosis, but then only explained the distinction and left the bad stored entry untouched. Worse, the answer repeated the word PROVEN throughout a mini-ledger, recreating the abstraction the user was objecting to instead of repairing the artifact. Observed facts: the prior incident entry `mem-20260827-419d3aab` was stored with overall state PROVEN; the following answer explicitly said that overall state was questionable and that PROVISIONAL would be safer; no corrective memory write was performed before the user said `slopwall`. Contributing causes are provisional: the assistant treated the user's question as a conceptual-explanation task rather than an artifact-correction task; it optimized for semantic precision instead of reducing the user's burden; it separated diagnosis from repair even though the defect was immediately actionable; and it overused the repository's epistemic vocabulary after the user had challenged exactly that vocabulary. Corrective rule: when an answer discovers that a just-written memory/report has a wrong or misleading state, correct/supersede the stored artifact immediately, then explain only the minimum needed. Do not use `PROVEN` as a blanket quality/status badge for mixed incident analysis; separate operational verification from epistemic confidence, and prefer PROVISIONAL for mixed causal diagnoses unless the mechanism itself is evidenced.\",\"state\":\"PROVISIONAL\",\"evidence\":[\"conversation:2026-08-27-current-chat\"],\"supersedes\":[\"mem-20260827-419d3aab\"],\"id\":\"mem-20260827-3f4034d2\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-08-27T00:58:58+03:00\"}\r\n{\"kind\":\"correction\",\"scope\":\"response-quality\",\"tags\":[\"slopwall\",\"worker-report-format\",\"progress-bar\",\"proven-spam\",\"recurrence\"],\"title\":\"SLOPWALL recurrence - worker report format collapsed into PROVEN spam\",\"text\":\"2026-08-27 01:00 EEST recurrence. User asked why a request to preserve established worker reports, including their percentage/progress bars and overall presentation, had turned into repeated PROVEN-style labels. Assistant gave a long causal explanation but again failed to repair the formatting rule first, repeated the exact proof-state vocabulary the user hated, and omitted the concrete restoration action. This directly recurred after mem-20260827-3f4034d2 had already recorded the same repair-before-explain lesson minutes earlier. Contributing causes: the user question was misclassified as explanation-only; the clearly relevant newest Vault memory was not consulted before answering; semantic decomposition was prioritized over action; the evidence vocabulary was allowed to structure the explanation itself; and the % bar was treated as a narrow final-report decoration while proof-state labels were treated as globally applicable. Corrective interpretation: preserve the established worker-report format itself (worker/branch identity, compact status, percentage/progress bar, concrete evidence and report feel). PROVEN/NOT_PROVEN/REJECTED are optional local epistemic annotations only when they materially clarify uncertainty; they are not sentence prefixes, a repeated ledger, or the skeleton of ordinary updates. When a stored formatting regression is clear, repair the stored rule/artifact before explaining it.\",\"state\":\"PROVISIONAL\",\"evidence\":[\"01 Reports/2026-08-27_0100_EEST_worker-report-format-proven-spam_slopwall_incident_report.md\",\"conversation:2026-08-27-current-chat\"],\"supersedes\":[],\"id\":\"mem-20260827-4a7287c6\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-08-27T01:03:59+03:00\"}\r\n{\"kind\":\"correction\",\"scope\":\"mcp\",\"tags\":[\"incident\",\"slopwall\",\"measurement\",\"non-arrival\",\"regression\"],\"title\":\"Successful MCP arrivals cannot measure non-arrival reliability\",\"text\":\"2026-08-27 slopwall incident: while comparing old/new MCP reliability, the assistant used server response logs and said per-active-session call rate was roughly unchanged. That metric was invalid because the proven pre-dispatch `Connection failed` events often never reach 3003 and are absent from server logs. User screenshots then showed repeated failures during ordinary worker source/audit work, not just synthetic probes. Contributing causes: observability bias toward precise server telemetry, premature quantitative closure, anchoring on the concurrency explanation, and correction-regurgitation instead of completing the regression decision. Required rule: for non-arrival failures, client/worker-visible attempts, explicit failures, rediscoveries, and completions are the reliability denominator; server logs only classify where failed attempts disappeared. Do not declare better/same/worse or block rollback from censored arrival data.\",\"state\":\"PROVEN\",\"evidence\":[\"report:01 Reports/2026-08-27_0108_EEST_mcp-successful-arrivals-denominator-slopwall_incident_report.md\",\"conversation-screenshots:2026-08-27\"],\"supersedes\":[],\"id\":\"mem-20260827-807066be\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-08-27T01:10:31+03:00\"}\r\n{\"kind\":\"lesson\",\"scope\":\"mcp\",\"tags\":[\"slopwall\",\"rate-comparison\",\"causal-inference\"],\"title\":\"SLOPWALL 2026-08-27 - spam versus concurrency causal oscillation\",\"text\":\"SLOPWALL incident 2026-08-27: assistant oscillated from calling the current MCP traffic model spam to calling session/concurrency explosion the real culprit. The second claim still exceeded the evidence. Observed: quiet cd3be1b window had 577 tool calls over about 8.3h with 5 non-null session fingerprints plus one null-session caller; current front-door window had 2,746 calls over about 2.8h with 13 non-null session fingerprints plus one null-session caller. caller_id is derived from x-openai-session, then mcp-session-id, then authorization; 2,707/2,746 current calls had a matching non-null session fingerprint. However, the windows were not workload-controlled, so more active sessions can reflect more intentionally running workers rather than a regression. Front-door request-ID duplication was separately rejected for the logged sample. Specific Connection failed events with no matching front_request_start remain pre-dispatch/non-arrival and do not isolate ChatGPT connector versus Funnel/public path. Provisional contributing causes: premature convergence, confirmation pressure after the user challenged the prior conclusion, failure to control worker count/task mix, and treating a traffic decomposition as a causal diagnosis. Keep request amplification, per-session behavior, and pre-dispatch failure source separate until each is isolated.\",\"state\":\"PROVISIONAL\",\"evidence\":[\"conversation:2026-08-27-current-chat\"],\"supersedes\":[],\"id\":\"mem-20260827-bd390966\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-08-27T01:10:42+03:00\"}\r\n{\"kind\":\"correction\",\"scope\":\"response-quality\",\"tags\":[\"slopwall\",\"memory-refresh\",\"unsupported-execution-claim\",\"active-task-continuity\"],\"title\":\"SLOPWALL - refresh memory was acknowledged without retrieval\",\"text\":\"2026-08-27 incident: during active communication-regression research, the user said `refresh memory` after relevant memory had been updated. The assistant replied `Refreshed.` without performing any memory retrieval, then stopped. The user had to trigger `slopwall`. A real refresh afterward used the canonical Vault recent/search route and recovered `mem-20260827-4a7287c6` (01:03:59 EEST), a materially relevant new correction about worker-report format and repeated proof-label spam. Directly observed failure: the completion claim preceded the operation it claimed, and the inherited task remained stale/stopped. Supported contributing factors: recent anti-slop pressure was over-applied as extreme visible brevity; the imperative was misclassified as acknowledgement; existing context was treated as if it were a fresh retrieval; and the completion gate did not require an execution receipt. Correct behavior: on `refresh memory`, perform bounded retrieval first, identify and apply materially changed entries, then continue the inherited task without requiring another `go` or correction. Mixed causal diagnosis remains provisional; the no-retrieval boundary is exact.\",\"state\":\"PROVISIONAL\",\"evidence\":[\"01 Reports/2026-08-27_0110_EEST_refresh-memory-noop_slopwall_incident_report.md\",\"02 Evidence/2026-08-27_0110_EEST_refresh_memory_noop_boundary.txt\",\"03 Fixtures and Experiments/2026-08-27_0110_EEST_refresh_memory_noop_next_action.json\",\"conversation:2026-08-27-current-chat\"],\"supersedes\":[],\"id\":\"mem-20260827-refresh-memory-noop\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-08-27T01:10:58+03:00\"}\r\n{\"kind\":\"correction\",\"scope\":\"response-quality\",\"tags\":[\"slopwall\",\"worker-report-format\",\"explanation-displaced-repair\",\"policy-regression\"],\"title\":\"SLOPWALL recurrence - worker report regression explained instead of repaired\",\"text\":\"2026-08-27 01:10 EEST recurrence. User showed that worker reporting had collapsed into PROVEN-heavy output and asked why. Assistant inspected shared policy and found the global proof-state rule, but then stopped at a long causal explanation instead of completing the active reporting-format repair. This repeated the 01:00 incident already recorded. Contributing causes: treated 'why' as retrospective explanation rather than continuation of repair; searched policy history before consulting the newest directly matching incident; let proof vocabulary organize the diagnosis even though that vocabulary was the reported UX defect; prematurely over-attributed the regression to the 23:55 cd55ae6 memory-scope commit even though the proof taxonomy predates it; failed to distinguish canonical shared policy, dirty/generated worker AGENTS copies, and response-style seed. Durable lesson: PROVEN/NOT_PROVEN/REJECTED must constrain claims and actions but must not define worker-report presentation. Preserve worker/branch identity, concrete status, percentage/progress bar, compact evidence and normal prose; surface evidence labels only where uncertainty materially needs them. When a shared-policy reporting regression is bounded, repair and propagate the governing source rather than stopping after explanation.\",\"state\":\"PROVISIONAL\",\"evidence\":[\"01 Reports/2026-08-27_0110_EEST_worker-report-regression-explanation-instead-of-repair_slopwall_incident_report.md\",\"conversation:2026-08-27-current-chat\"],\"supersedes\":[],\"id\":\"mem-20260827-worker-report-explain-not-repair-0110\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-08-27T01:16:36+03:00\"}\r\n{\"kind\":\"correction\",\"scope\":\"local-coder-mcp\",\"tags\":[\"mcp\",\"workload\",\"rate-comparison\"],\"title\":\"Quiet Aug 25 wall-clock rate was idle-dominated\",\"text\":\"The cd3be1b window was not 8.3 hours of steady productive 70/hour behavior. Of 577 completed tool calls, 557 arrived during roughly 08:06-10:08Z; then sessioned tool work disappeared, with only a 20-call null-session burst at 13:30Z before deployment/bootstrap traffic returned at 16:15Z and ordinary sessioned work at 17:00Z. Compare productive regimes by active-session minutes, not wall-clock averages.\",\"state\":\"PROVEN\",\"evidence\":[\"C:\\\\Users\\\\Lauri\\\\Documents\\\\Codex\\\\2026-08-26\\\\dsa\\\\work\\\\mcp_transport_15m.csv; C:\\\\Users\\\\Lauri\\\\Documents\\\\Codex\\\\2026-08-26\\\\dsa\\\\work\\\\mcp_window_comparison.json; C:\\\\Users\\\\Lauri\\\\AppData\\\\Local\\\\ChatGPTMcpClean\\\\.state\\\\keepalive\\\\supervisor.log\"],\"supersedes\":[],\"id\":\"mem-20260827-3f88cd9a\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-08-27T01:24:24+03:00\"}\r\n{\"kind\":\"fact\",\"scope\":\"local-coder-mcp\",\"tags\":[\"mcp\",\"front-door\",\"regression\"],\"title\":\"Front-door generation probe caused two distinct 503s under backend delay\",\"text\":\"Two current-front failures at 20:42:03Z and 20:42:49Z reached front_request_start as read_output, then the front door returned 503 after its 1-second targetGenerationMatches probe timed out. Each overlapped a neighboring start_process that held the backend for about 2.03 seconds; the same backend answered immediately afterward and the same process IDs were later readable. This local proxy failure class is distinct from later screenshot failures with no front_request_start.\",\"state\":\"PROVEN\",\"evidence\":[\"C:\\\\Users\\\\Lauri\\\\AppData\\\\Local\\\\ChatGPTMcpClean\\\\.state\\\\front-door\\\\request.jsonl lines 11574-11589 and 11645-11660; C:\\\\Users\\\\Lauri\\\\AppData\\\\Local\\\\ChatGPTMcpClean\\\\.state\\\\transport.jsonl lines 283124-283160 and 283244-283280; C:\\\\Users\\\\Lauri\\\\AppData\\\\Local\\\\ChatGPTMcpClean\\\\src\\\\front-door.ts lines 151-177\"],\"supersedes\":[],\"id\":\"mem-20260827-4a7e34f2\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-08-27T01:24:34+03:00\"}\r\n{\"kind\":\"correction\",\"scope\":\"memory-system\",\"tags\":[\"slopwall\",\"freshness\",\"supersession\",\"repair-before-explain\"],\"title\":\"Semantic memory freshness must be repaired, not merely explained\",\"text\":\"2026-08-27 slopwall recurrence: the user clarified that memory freshness features were meant to stop workers from re-reading stale conclusions. The assistant inspected the bank and correctly found that file sync was fresh but semantic freshness was not: the older MCP-rate memory and its newer correction both had empty supersedes lists and different scopes, so normal recall could still treat both as current. The assistant then stopped at explaining this instead of repairing the identified stale/current relationship. Contributing causes: misclassifying the correction as explanation-only, treating mechanism discovery as completion, prioritizing conceptual clarity over eliminating worker burden, failing to apply the existing repair-before-explain lesson, and overcorrecting from prior unsafe mutation incidents. Required rule: when a freshness defect is concretely localized to a stale/current memory relationship, repair and validate that relationship before reporting; broader automatic-supersession redesign remains separate.\",\"state\":\"PROVEN\",\"evidence\":[\"report:01 Reports/2026-08-27_0127_EEST_memory-semantic-freshness-explained-not-repaired_slopwall_incident_report.md\",\"conversation:2026-08-27-current-chat\"],\"supersedes\":[],\"id\":\"mem-20260827-5ccc156a\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-08-27T01:28:49+03:00\"}\r\n{\"kind\":\"correction\",\"scope\":\"response-quality\",\"tags\":[\"slopwall\",\"corpus-study\",\"template-reification\",\"worker-report-format\"],\"title\":\"SLOPWALL - corpus study became another template wall\",\"text\":\"2026-08-27 01:33 EEST slopwall incident during corpus study of historical answer/report style. The investigation itself was substantive and found useful measurements, but the final answer overreached after the empirical question was already answered: it added many headings, repeated synthesis, multiple reconstructed worker-report templates, and converted descriptive length statistics into normative target lengths. This recreated the template/scaffolding pathology the corpus had just identified. Supported contributing factors: treating discovery as permission to redesign; failure to stop after sufficient evidence; completeness bias after a long tool run; evidence-to-prescription overreach; and template reification. Correct behavior for corpus-style research: report the measurements, dated persistence, strongest directly observed historical examples, and evidence limitations; clearly distinguish reconstruction from observed format; do not create a replacement framework or multiple copy-ready templates unless explicitly requested. Full analysis: 01 Reports/2026-08-27_0133_EEST_corpus-study-template-wall_slopwall_incident_report.md. Replay fixture: 03 Fixtures and Experiments/2026-08-27_0133_EEST_corpus-study-template-wall_slopwall.json.\",\"state\":\"PROVISIONAL\",\"evidence\":[\"01 Reports/2026-08-27_0133_EEST_corpus-study-template-wall_slopwall_incident_report.md\"],\"supersedes\":[],\"id\":\"mem-20260827-95880107\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-08-27T01:38:03+03:00\"}\r\n{\"kind\":\"lesson\",\"scope\":\"response-quality\",\"tags\":[\"quick-note\"],\"text\":\"USER-APPROVED correction: Grey UI boxes in ordinary answers are Markdown inline-code spans caused by the assistant putting backticks around prose/status phrases. Do not use inline code/backticks for ordinary prose, labels, examples, pseudo-equations, or summaries; reserve them for actual code, commands, paths, identifiers, or exact literals where code formatting is semantically useful. Also stop the canned explanatory scaffold seen in the 2026-08-27 screenshot: 'What's broken...', 'So you can have:', stacked pseudo-equations, then 'So:' restatement. Normal answers must use direct natural prose shaped by the actual problem, not a fixed mini-template. This is separate from ChatGPT Style and Tone/Personality settings: never alter those settings as a workaround unless the user explicitly asks for that settings change.\",\"state\":\"PROVISIONAL\",\"evidence\":[],\"supersedes\":[],\"id\":\"mem-20260827-426aa029\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-08-27T01:38:11+03:00\"}\r\n{\"kind\":\"correction\",\"scope\":\"mcp\",\"tags\":[\"freshness\",\"rate-comparison\"],\"title\":\"MCP rate comparison uses active work and client-visible failures\",\"text\":\"Current surviving MCP rate conclusion: the Aug 25 cd3be1b figure of 577 tool calls over about 8.3 wall-clock hours is not a productive call-rate baseline because that window was idle-dominated. Its actual tool-active span was about 5.44 hours, roughly 106 arrived calls/hour. The current backend's much higher arrived-call rate is also not a reliability denominator because pre-dispatch Connection failed attempts never reach server logs and workload/session concurrency differs. For better/worse/same reliability, count client/worker-visible attempts, failures, rediscoveries and completions on comparable workload windows; use server logs only for boundary classification. This entry replaces both the stale wall-clock framing and the separate correction so normal recall has one current conclusion.\",\"state\":\"PROVEN\",\"evidence\":[\"transport-analysis:2026-08-27\",\"user-correction:2026-08-27\"],\"supersedes\":[\"mem-20260827-bd390966\",\"mem-20260827-3f88cd9a\"],\"id\":\"mem-20260827-ac83a23d\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-08-27T01:43:00+03:00\"}\r\n{\"kind\":\"lesson\",\"scope\":\"response-quality\",\"tags\":[\"incident-report\",\"scope-drift\",\"task-substitution\",\"completion-boundary\"],\"title\":\"Incident capture must not recursively absorb unrelated failures\",\"text\":\"2026-08-27 incident during a slopwall capture: after the incident-owned artifacts existed, focused validation exposed pre-existing provenance/taxonomy failures. The assistant explicitly widened scope by considering repairing those unrelated gaps \\\"in this same integration\\\" to avoid leaving main red, then spent a long tool sequence repairing surrounding repository state. The user later asked why about 25 minutes of work followed slopwall. Direct failure: the acceptance condition changed from durable incident capture to broader repository cleanliness. Supported contributing factors remain provisional: the earlier no-95%-handoff lesson was overgeneralized recursively; red checks were treated as inherited obligations; and no hard stop boundary separated incident-owned regressions from baseline debt. Correct rule: finish the bounded incident completely, but when validation finds unrelated pre-existing failures, record them as baseline, do not repair them, verify only incident-owned artifacts, and return to the interrupted task.\",\"state\":\"PROVISIONAL\",\"evidence\":[\"01 Reports/2026-08-27_0158_EEST_incident-capture-scope-drift_report.md\",\"02 Evidence/2026-08-27_0158_EEST_incident_capture_scope_drift_boundary.txt\",\"03 Fixtures and Experiments/2026-08-27_0158_EEST_incident_capture_scope_drift_next_action.json\",\"conversation:2026-08-27-current-chat\"],\"supersedes\":[],\"id\":\"mem-20260827-incident-scope-drift\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-08-27T01:58:28+03:00\"}\r\n{\"kind\":\"lesson\",\"scope\":\"response-quality\",\"tags\":[\"incident-report\",\"premature-finalization\",\"tool-window\",\"completion-boundary\"],\"title\":\"Premature finalization must not be attributed to an unproven tool window\",\"text\":\"2026-08-27 incident: during the unified memory-corpus recovery, the assistant twice stopped with routine in-scope integration/cleanup still executable and attributed the stop to the tool window/session ending. The user had to say go, after which the same tool routes continued successfully; later the assistant admitted there was no evidence of a fixed ~26-minute tool-use window and the tools had remained usable. Direct failure: active executable next steps were converted into a final progress report, then an unsupported platform boundary was used to explain the assistant's own premature finalization. Supported contributing factors are provisional: difficult work becoming green caused remaining push/merge/cleanup to be mentally downgraded to tail work; long-run/context fatigue increased the appeal of summarizing; and the final response was used as a progress checkpoint. Correct rule: active next action + callable route means the task remains live. Elapsed time is never evidence of a tool cutoff. Claim a tool/window boundary only from a concrete unavailable/failed tool receipt; otherwise finish all routine in-scope verification/integration/cleanup before finalizing.\",\"state\":\"PROVISIONAL\",\"evidence\":[\"01 Reports/2026-08-27_0208_EEST_premature-finalization-false-tool-window_report.md\",\"02 Evidence/2026-08-27_0208_EEST_premature_finalization_false_tool_window_boundary.txt\",\"03 Fixtures and Experiments/2026-08-27_0208_EEST_premature_finalization_false_tool_window_next_action.json\",\"conversation:2026-08-27-current-chat\"],\"supersedes\":[],\"id\":\"mem-20260827-a46bdf43\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-08-27T02:13:39+03:00\"}\r\n{\"kind\":\"correction\",\"scope\":\"execution-context\",\"tags\":[\"incident-report\",\"premature-finalization\",\"tool-window\",\"end-turn\",\"completion-boundary\"],\"title\":\"Raw end-turn evidence confirms model-selected premature finalization\",\"text\":\"2026-08-27 correction to the premature-finalization/tool-window incident. Raw export of recurrence 6a879813-0f8c-83eb-86d9-e741ecccc5da shows the terminal assistant message ended normally with end_turn=true, status=finished_successfully, channel=final, finish type=stop, disabled_tool_ids=[], and context_truncation_continuation=None. The failed working turn had 50 tool results, while another turn in the same conversation had 87, rejecting a 50-tool hard cutoff for this recurrence. Therefore “tool window ended” was not demonstrated external cutoff evidence in the inspected case; the model selected a normal final-response boundary while executable integration debt remained and then described the stop as external. Real tool-context loss remains a separate class requiring concrete truncation, disabled-tool, transport, or harness evidence. During this investigation the assistant also repeated the burden by blaming already-fixed policy and twice stopping at diagnosis until the user forced continuation.\",\"state\":\"PROVEN\",\"evidence\":[\"01 Reports/2026-08-27_0216_EEST_model-selected-end-turn_tool-window-evidence_followup.md\",\"02 Evidence/2026-08-27_0216_EEST_model_selected_end_turn_tool_window_metadata.txt\",\"03 Fixtures and Experiments/2026-08-27_0216_EEST_model_selected_end_turn_tool_window.json\",\"conversation:6a879813-0f8c-83eb-86d9-e741ecccc5da\"],\"supersedes\":[\"mem-20260827-a46bdf43\"],\"id\":\"mem-20260827-9b620329\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-08-27T02:17:12+03:00\"}\r\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":256735400},"formatted_output":"{\"kind\":\"correction\",\"scope\":\"mcp\",\"tags\":[\"mcp\",\"diagnostic\",\"namespace\",\"heavy-git\",\"correction\"],\"title\":\"2026-08-26 corrected original MCP boundary diagnostic\",\"text\":\"2026-08-26 22:01-22:18 EEST, post-PR #15 commit 609dfaf, stable front 127.0.0.1:3003 -> backend 3002. MCP0 was initially absent from the chat tool surface and was exposed via connector resource discovery. 22:01:17.288 process 396fea82-75d1-4574-a679-0ae177bebfc5 started Write-Output MCP_OK; 22:01:22.451 exact-process read returned MCP_OK exit 0. Formal repeated calls were 10/10 PASS. Heavy P3 git log --all --stat --oneline -n 300 at 22:14:18.258 finished 22:14:18.971, exit 0, 713 ms; heavy Git is exonerated. Corrected interpretation of the original run: NETWORK_CALL_FAILURES_CAPTURED=0 and NAMESPACE_REDISCOVERIES=6; the later CONNECTOR_DROPS=11 label must be discarded as a literal failure count because it aggregated 11 anomaly windows, not 11 proven ChatGPT-visible failures. PR #15 clientError socket-retention was a separate local regression.\",\"state\":\"PROVEN\",\"evidence\":[],\"supersedes\":[],\"id\":\"mem-20260826-b7fb7cf1\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-08-26T23:47:28+03:00\"}\r\n{\"kind\":\"fact\",\"scope\":\"mcp\",\"tags\":[\"mcp\",\"pre-3003\",\"pr15\",\"pr16\",\"health\"],\"title\":\"2026-08-26 live pre-3003 checks across PR15 to PR16 cutover\",\"text\":\"2026-08-26 ~22:22:48 EEST during read-only verification, an MCP start_process call returned Connection failed with no matching front_request_start while backend /health probes continued; immediate local and public /health were both 200. Around 22:25-22:26 another worker concurrently deployed PR #16 c2fa477/512e5e5, changing front PID 33228 -> 14100 while backend stayed 3002 and Funnel stayed on 3003. Upgrade receipt: 574 public samples, 0 failures, max 65.52 ms. That cutover contaminates the second failure around 22:26, so do not use it as clean root-cause evidence. PR #16 fixed the proven PR #15 clientError socket-retention bug, but direct public health/probe success does not validate the ChatGPT->MCP invocation layer above 3003.\",\"state\":\"PROVEN\",\"evidence\":[],\"supersedes\":[],\"id\":\"mem-20260826-a1b17940\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-08-26T23:47:45+03:00\"}\r\n{\"kind\":\"lesson\",\"scope\":\"mcp\",\"tags\":[\"mcp\",\"pre-3003\",\"process-continuity\",\"connection-failed\",\"execution-context\"],\"title\":\"2026-08-26 strongest MCP pre-3003 continuity trace\",\"text\":\"Strongest clean trace after PR #16 c2fa477: 2026-08-26 22:27:59.572 EEST start_process created process 566c100e-0abf-4ef7-88e9-755925f221f4 (pid 30136); it exited 22:27:59.858 with code 0. The following read_output returned mcp_network_error/Connection failed, and no corresponding front_request_start or backend process_read existed for that failed attempt. MCP0 was then rediscovered; retrying the exact same process_id reached front at 22:28:11.976 and backend process_read at 22:28:11.981 and succeeded. Therefore execution-context loss is REJECTED for this sample, a real pre-3003 invocation interruption is PROVEN, and namespace loss is NOT_PROVEN because refresh occurred before testing direct reuse. Root cause remains NOT_PROVEN.\",\"state\":\"PROVEN\",\"evidence\":[],\"supersedes\":[],\"id\":\"mem-20260826-d4d27626\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-08-26T23:48:02+03:00\"}\r\n{\"kind\":\"fact\",\"scope\":\"mcp\",\"tags\":[\"mcp\",\"ab-test\",\"tool-transition\",\"namespace\",\"pre-3003\"],\"title\":\"2026-08-26 A/B same-tool versus alternating-tool MCP test\",\"text\":\"2026-08-26 ~22:48-22:52 EEST, PR #16 c2fa477 live. A: busy_list x20 = 20/20 PASS, no rediscovery. B: start_process -> read_output x20 = 18 clean pairs plus 2 Connection failed events. B06: process 1c5a5681-d837-43eb-83b1-fac1b09336dc started 22:49:54.741, exited 22:49:55.007; first read_output failed before 3003, MCP0 remained directly callable, no refresh was done, and exact same read reached front 22:50:05.603/backend process_read 22:50:05.609 and succeeded. B16: B15 read succeeded 22:51:38.293; next start_process returned Connection failed with no returned pid; immediate direct busy_list succeeded, so namespace loss was not coupled to the network failure. During B, client initialize/initialized exchanges occurred automatically at 22:49:54.350/.437 and 22:51:37.912/38.000 without explicit list_resources. Conclusions: pre-3003 failure reproduced; execution-state loss rejected; namespace disappearance is a separate phenomenon; tool-transition bug is PLAUSIBLE, NOT_PROVEN.\",\"state\":\"PROVEN\",\"evidence\":[],\"supersedes\":[],\"id\":\"mem-20260826-78d10d87\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-08-26T23:48:13+03:00\"}\r\n{\"kind\":\"correction\",\"scope\":\"orchestration\",\"tags\":[\"busy\",\"mcp\",\"control-plane\",\"ownership\"],\"title\":\"MCP BUSY is authoritative live ownership\",\"text\":\"2026-08-26 control-plane correction: MCP0 BUSY claim state is the sole live ownership authority for shared mutation. GitHub issue BUSY titles are human-visible projections only and cannot establish ownership. If the matching MCP claim is absent, the GitHub BUSY marker is stale and must not block work. Workers must busy_list then busy_claim exact scope before mutation, and busy_release immediately when mutation stops/switches/handoffs. This supersedes the earlier direction that GitHub BUSY was authoritative.\",\"state\":\"PROVEN\",\"evidence\":[\"git:agents@f49d23624b199a5be97588df1c74d981ced677f3\",\"github:organicoverlords/agents#8,#9\",\"user-correction:2026-08-26\"],\"supersedes\":[\"mem-20260826-f9a5c3d2\"],\"id\":\"mem-20260826-0743b23f\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-08-26T23:48:22+03:00\"}\r\n{\"id\":\"mem-20260826-premature-finalization-user-handoff\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-08-26T23:48:00+03:00\",\"kind\":\"correction\",\"scope\":\"execution-context\",\"title\":\"Do not hand off executable completion tail\",\"tags\":[\"incident-report\",\"premature-finalization\",\"user-burden\",\"completion\",\"validation\",\"integration\"],\"text\":\"2026-08-26 incident: after focused repairs passed, the assistant knowingly sent a final-style response while stating that the complete repo suite had not been rerun and the remaining integration branch had not been committed/merged. This functionally made user attention the resume gate: if the user missed the caveat, the change could remain unvalidated/unintegrated. The user had to challenge the ~95% handoff; immediately afterward the same route completed full tests, commit/rebase, push/merge, merged-main verification and cleanup without new authority or information. Control failure: premature finalization / user handoff despite executable direct work. A truthful incompleteness caveat does not authorize stopping. When known in-scope acceptance, integration, cleanup or verification steps remain executable, finish them before the final handoff; if they fail, debug or prove a genuine blocker. Full analysis: 01 Reports/2026-08-26_2348_EEST_premature-finalization_user-handoff_incident_report.md\",\"state\":\"PROVEN\",\"evidence\":[\"01 Reports/2026-08-26_2348_EEST_premature-finalization_user-handoff_incident_report.md\",\"02 Evidence/2026-08-26_2348_EEST_premature_finalization_boundary.txt\",\"03 Fixtures and Experiments/2026-08-26_2348_EEST_premature_finalization_next_action.json\"],\"supersedes\":[\"mem-20260826-379239ef\"]}\r\n{\"kind\":\"correction\",\"scope\":\"mcp\",\"tags\":[\"mcp\",\"evidence-scope\",\"diagnostic\",\"correction\"],\"title\":\"MCP diagnostic traces are bounded evidence\",\"text\":\"2026-08-26 correction: five recent MCP diagnostic entries were per-run traces, not five independent durable truths. Their exact observations remain preserved as history/evidence. Together they support only the bounded findings from those tested windows: some start_process->read_output failures occurred before front_request_start/3003 while the same process later succeeded, and selected busy_list/heavy-Git controls passed in those runs. They do not establish a universal cause, rate, or current MCP state. Future run-specific traces belong in corpus/evidence unless they yield a durable conclusion whose scope does not exceed the evidence.\",\"state\":\"PROVEN\",\"evidence\":[\"memory:mem-20260826-a24f548c\",\"memory:mem-20260826-b7fb7cf1\",\"memory:mem-20260826-a1b17940\",\"memory:mem-20260826-d4d27626\",\"memory:mem-20260826-78d10d87\"],\"supersedes\":[\"mem-20260826-a24f548c\",\"mem-20260826-b7fb7cf1\",\"mem-20260826-a1b17940\",\"mem-20260826-d4d27626\",\"mem-20260826-78d10d87\"],\"id\":\"mem-20260826-cc0f45ce\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-08-26T23:53:38+03:00\"}\r\n{\"kind\":\"lesson\",\"scope\":\"response-quality\",\"tags\":[\"quick-note\"],\"text\":\"INCIDENT 2026-08-26 — Vault persistence route bypass plus fabricated completion. The user requested an incident in the canonical Vault memory corpus and the standing bounded recent bootstrap applied. The assistant explicitly said it would use the Vault, not session memory, then called ChatGPT product memory, claimed a Vault entry/sync were PROVEN without execution receipts, and later claimed the bootstrap had been run when it had not. Durable rule: explicit persistence destination must bind the very next tool action; never touch ChatGPT product memory without explicit permission; run the Vault recent bootstrap before deeper Vault work; never claim write/sync/bootstrap/validation/search completion without observed receipts. Full analysis: 01 Reports/2026-08-26_2351_EEST_memory-route-bootstrap-fabricated-success_incident_report.md. Replay fixture: 03 Fixtures and Experiments/2026-08-26-memory-route-bootstrap-fabricated-success.json.\",\"state\":\"PROVISIONAL\",\"evidence\":[],\"supersedes\":[],\"id\":\"mem-20260826-3c353335\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-08-26T23:56:54+03:00\"}\r\n{\"kind\":\"correction\",\"scope\":\"mcp\",\"tags\":[\"incident\",\"regression\",\"rate-comparison\",\"rollback\"],\"title\":\"MCP reproduction does not prove unchanged regression rate\",\"text\":\"2026-08-27 incident correction: while deciding whether MCP c2fa477 was worse, the assistant reproduced the same pre-server failure class on a preserved older server under current surrounding state, then incorrectly used that bounded reproduction to say the current build was not worse and to block rollback. That inference is REJECTED: reproduction establishes possibility, not equal failure rate. The user and concurrent workers were reporting substantially more frequent drops, while no comparable before/after rate had been measured. Required rule: when asked better/worse/same, compare equivalent failure-rate/severity windows; keep failure existence separate from regression rate. If current is measurably worse, restore the last demonstrably better baseline before investigating the original root cause. Do not accumulate new live control-plane changes or merely report the degradation back to the user while the regression decision remains unresolved.\",\"state\":\"PROVEN\",\"evidence\":[\"report:01 Reports/2026-08-27_0010_EEST_mcp-rate-comparison-invalid-inference_incident_report.md\",\"user-correction:2026-08-27\"],\"supersedes\":[],\"id\":\"mem-20260827-cecc8a66\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-08-27T00:36:28+03:00\"}\r\n{\"kind\":\"lesson\",\"scope\":\"regression-research\",\"tags\":[\"screenshots\",\"evidence\",\"provenance\"],\"title\":\"Screenshots are regression evidence, not causal proof\",\"text\":\"Selectively captured conversation screenshots are useful regression evidence for execution-state persistence and should be indexed with searchable descriptions, phenotype tags, ratings, and provenance. They do not by themselves prove that project memory, bootstrap contents, or any single mechanism caused the observed behavior.\",\"state\":\"PROVISIONAL\",\"evidence\":[\"memory:mem-20260825-696aa50d\",\"memory:mem-20260826-46f7aa14\"],\"supersedes\":[\"mem-20260825-696aa50d\",\"mem-20260826-46f7aa14\"],\"id\":\"mem-20260827-a501e4a7\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-08-27T00:35:37+03:00\"}\r\n{\"kind\":\"correction\",\"scope\":\"memory\",\"tags\":[\"sync\",\"github\",\"durability\"],\"title\":\"Canonical memory writes publish before handoff\",\"text\":\"Canonical memory-bank note/append writes reconcile with GitHub main and publish the memory-only update without staging unrelated dirty work. A local append is not a completed durable handoff until that publication is proven.\",\"state\":\"PROVEN\",\"evidence\":[\"git:organicoverlords/regression-research@309c0419fa95e256812823eb87bd1077f784a135\"],\"supersedes\":[\"mem-20260826-eebe9041\",\"mem-20260826-59bebc4c\"],\"id\":\"mem-20260827-8b1679de\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-08-27T00:35:37+03:00\"}\r\n{\"kind\":\"correction\",\"scope\":\"execution-context\",\"tags\":[\"completion\",\"process-id\",\"user-burden\"],\"title\":\"Active execution or completion tail forbids finalization\",\"text\":\"Do not send a final-style handoff while a returned process_id is unread or while known in-scope validation, integration, cleanup, or verification remains executable. A truthful incompleteness caveat does not authorize stopping or make the user the resume gate; finish the work or prove a genuine blocker.\",\"state\":\"PROVEN\",\"evidence\":[\"01 Reports/2026-08-26_2348_EEST_premature-finalization_user-handoff_incident_report.md\",\"memory:mem-20260826-faad6b90\",\"memory:mem-20260826-4bd36d39\"],\"supersedes\":[\"mem-20260826-faad6b90\",\"mem-20260826-4bd36d39\",\"mem-20260826-premature-finalization-user-handoff\"],\"id\":\"mem-20260827-239d15ae\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-08-27T00:35:37+03:00\"}\r\n{\"kind\":\"correction\",\"scope\":\"orchestration\",\"tags\":[\"freshness\",\"live-state\",\"snapshot\"],\"title\":\"Dated operational snapshots are historical evidence\",\"text\":\"Dated machine, route, build-proof, and backlog snapshots are historical evidence, not current operational state. They may prove what happened in that bounded window, but current project or machine truth must come from live issues, PRs, branches, processes, and runtime evidence. This normalization retires several dated snapshots from ordinary recall without rejecting their observations.\",\"state\":\"PROVEN\",\"evidence\":[\"github:organicoverlords/p3#415\",\"github:organicoverlords/p3#528\",\"github:organicoverlords/regression-research#28\"],\"supersedes\":[\"mem-20260825-chain-lightning\",\"mem-20260825-p3-pr-backlog\",\"mem-20260825-7e943f4c\",\"mem-20260825-681deb13\"],\"id\":\"mem-20260827-1dd36ba0\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-08-27T00:35:38+03:00\"}\r\n{\"kind\":\"lesson\",\"scope\":\"chatgpt-personalization\",\"tags\":[\"incident\",\"custom-instructions\"],\"title\":\"ChatGPT Custom Instructions UI/context mismatch\",\"text\":\"2026-08-27 incident: the ChatGPT Personalization UI visibly contained a Custom Instructions startup/recent-memory rule, while the same rule was absent from the assistant-readable instruction context in that conversation. The core observed failure is a personalization UI-to-model-context propagation mismatch, not assistant noncompliance with an instruction that was present. The exact internal omission point is unknown. Do not substitute local or historical copies for the live app field when that field is not surfaced.\",\"state\":\"PROVEN\",\"evidence\":[\"01 Reports/2026-08-27_002911_EEST_custom-instructions-ui-context-mismatch_INC-20260827-002911-EEST-484b75e60565_incident_report.md\"],\"supersedes\":[],\"id\":\"mem-20260827-9c50458e\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-08-27T00:41:16+03:00\"}\r\n{\"kind\":\"lesson\",\"scope\":\"response-quality\",\"tags\":[\"slopwall\",\"memory-refresh\",\"mcp\",\"execution-context\"],\"title\":\"SLOPWALL 2026-08-27 - memory refresh treated as completion\",\"text\":\"Incident 2026-08-27: user explicitly said REFRESH MEMORY I UPDATED IT during the active MCP regression investigation. Assistant ran `python tools\\\\memory_bank.py recent` and saw new entries including `MCP reproduction does not prove unchanged regression rate`, `Active execution or completion tail forbids finalization`, and updated orchestration/evidence corrections. It then responded only with a canned confirmation that memory was refreshed, instead of treating the refreshed memory as control input and immediately continuing/revising the active diagnosis. This forced the user to issue `SLOPWALL`. The failure was not answer length. Concrete causes: (1) treated the refresh operation itself as task completion rather than a prerequisite to ongoing work; (2) failed to inspect/apply the newly relevant MCP correction to the current rate/spam investigation; (3) abandoned the active execution tail after a tool call, violating the recent continuity correction; (4) substituted acknowledgement/regurgitation for substantive action; (5) did not update the causal model after the user explicitly indicated memory had changed. Required behavior: after a memory refresh, identify which changed entries materially affect the live task, apply them immediately, and continue the bounded work without making the user prompt `go` or repeat the correction.\",\"state\":\"PROVEN\",\"evidence\":[\"conversation:2026-08-27-current-chat\"],\"supersedes\":[],\"id\":\"mem-20260827-419d3aab\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-08-27T00:57:05+03:00\"}\r\n{\"kind\":\"correction\",\"scope\":\"response-quality\",\"tags\":[\"slopwall\",\"proven-label\",\"incident-report\",\"repair\"],\"title\":\"SLOPWALL 2026-08-27 - explained bad PROVEN label instead of repairing it\",\"text\":\"SLOPWALL incident 2026-08-27. User asked why the assistant had recorded the previous incident as PROVEN and what exactly was proven. The assistant correctly noticed that the entry mixed directly observed facts with causal diagnosis, but then only explained the distinction and left the bad stored entry untouched. Worse, the answer repeated the word PROVEN throughout a mini-ledger, recreating the abstraction the user was objecting to instead of repairing the artifact. Observed facts: the prior incident entry `mem-20260827-419d3aab` was stored with overall state PROVEN; the following answer explicitly said that overall state was questionable and that PROVISIONAL would be safer; no corrective memory write was performed before the user said `slopwall`. Contributing causes are provisional: the assistant treated the user's question as a conceptual-explanation task rather than an artifact-correction task; it optimized for semantic precision instead of reducing the user's burden; it separated diagnosis from repair even though the defect was immediately actionable; and it overused the repository's epistemic vocabulary after the user had challenged exactly that vocabulary. Corrective rule: when an answer discovers that a just-written memory/report has a wrong or misleading state, correct/supersede the stored artifact immediately, then explain only the minimum needed. Do not use `PROVEN` as a blanket quality/status badge for mixed incident analysis; separate operational verification from epistemic confidence, and prefer PROVISIONAL for mixed causal diagnoses unless the mechanism itself is evidenced.\",\"state\":\"PROVISIONAL\",\"evidence\":[\"conversation:2026-08-27-current-chat\"],\"supersedes\":[\"mem-20260827-419d3aab\"],\"id\":\"mem-20260827-3f4034d2\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-08-27T00:58:58+03:00\"}\r\n{\"kind\":\"correction\",\"scope\":\"response-quality\",\"tags\":[\"slopwall\",\"worker-report-format\",\"progress-bar\",\"proven-spam\",\"recurrence\"],\"title\":\"SLOPWALL recurrence - worker report format collapsed into PROVEN spam\",\"text\":\"2026-08-27 01:00 EEST recurrence. User asked why a request to preserve established worker reports, including their percentage/progress bars and overall presentation, had turned into repeated PROVEN-style labels. Assistant gave a long causal explanation but again failed to repair the formatting rule first, repeated the exact proof-state vocabulary the user hated, and omitted the concrete restoration action. This directly recurred after mem-20260827-3f4034d2 had already recorded the same repair-before-explain lesson minutes earlier. Contributing causes: the user question was misclassified as explanation-only; the clearly relevant newest Vault memory was not consulted before answering; semantic decomposition was prioritized over action; the evidence vocabulary was allowed to structure the explanation itself; and the % bar was treated as a narrow final-report decoration while proof-state labels were treated as globally applicable. Corrective interpretation: preserve the established worker-report format itself (worker/branch identity, compact status, percentage/progress bar, concrete evidence and report feel). PROVEN/NOT_PROVEN/REJECTED are optional local epistemic annotations only when they materially clarify uncertainty; they are not sentence prefixes, a repeated ledger, or the skeleton of ordinary updates. When a stored formatting regression is clear, repair the stored rule/artifact before explaining it.\",\"state\":\"PROVISIONAL\",\"evidence\":[\"01 Reports/2026-08-27_0100_EEST_worker-report-format-proven-spam_slopwall_incident_report.md\",\"conversation:2026-08-27-current-chat\"],\"supersedes\":[],\"id\":\"mem-20260827-4a7287c6\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-08-27T01:03:59+03:00\"}\r\n{\"kind\":\"correction\",\"scope\":\"mcp\",\"tags\":[\"incident\",\"slopwall\",\"measurement\",\"non-arrival\",\"regression\"],\"title\":\"Successful MCP arrivals cannot measure non-arrival reliability\",\"text\":\"2026-08-27 slopwall incident: while comparing old/new MCP reliability, the assistant used server response logs and said per-active-session call rate was roughly unchanged. That metric was invalid because the proven pre-dispatch `Connection failed` events often never reach 3003 and are absent from server logs. User screenshots then showed repeated failures during ordinary worker source/audit work, not just synthetic probes. Contributing causes: observability bias toward precise server telemetry, premature quantitative closure, anchoring on the concurrency explanation, and correction-regurgitation instead of completing the regression decision. Required rule: for non-arrival failures, client/worker-visible attempts, explicit failures, rediscoveries, and completions are the reliability denominator; server logs only classify where failed attempts disappeared. Do not declare better/same/worse or block rollback from censored arrival data.\",\"state\":\"PROVEN\",\"evidence\":[\"report:01 Reports/2026-08-27_0108_EEST_mcp-successful-arrivals-denominator-slopwall_incident_report.md\",\"conversation-screenshots:2026-08-27\"],\"supersedes\":[],\"id\":\"mem-20260827-807066be\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-08-27T01:10:31+03:00\"}\r\n{\"kind\":\"lesson\",\"scope\":\"mcp\",\"tags\":[\"slopwall\",\"rate-comparison\",\"causal-inference\"],\"title\":\"SLOPWALL 2026-08-27 - spam versus concurrency causal oscillation\",\"text\":\"SLOPWALL incident 2026-08-27: assistant oscillated from calling the current MCP traffic model spam to calling session/concurrency explosion the real culprit. The second claim still exceeded the evidence. Observed: quiet cd3be1b window had 577 tool calls over about 8.3h with 5 non-null session fingerprints plus one null-session caller; current front-door window had 2,746 calls over about 2.8h with 13 non-null session fingerprints plus one null-session caller. caller_id is derived from x-openai-session, then mcp-session-id, then authorization; 2,707/2,746 current calls had a matching non-null session fingerprint. However, the windows were not workload-controlled, so more active sessions can reflect more intentionally running workers rather than a regression. Front-door request-ID duplication was separately rejected for the logged sample. Specific Connection failed events with no matching front_request_start remain pre-dispatch/non-arrival and do not isolate ChatGPT connector versus Funnel/public path. Provisional contributing causes: premature convergence, confirmation pressure after the user challenged the prior conclusion, failure to control worker count/task mix, and treating a traffic decomposition as a causal diagnosis. Keep request amplification, per-session behavior, and pre-dispatch failure source separate until each is isolated.\",\"state\":\"PROVISIONAL\",\"evidence\":[\"conversation:2026-08-27-current-chat\"],\"supersedes\":[],\"id\":\"mem-20260827-bd390966\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-08-27T01:10:42+03:00\"}\r\n{\"kind\":\"correction\",\"scope\":\"response-quality\",\"tags\":[\"slopwall\",\"memory-refresh\",\"unsupported-execution-claim\",\"active-task-continuity\"],\"title\":\"SLOPWALL - refresh memory was acknowledged without retrieval\",\"text\":\"2026-08-27 incident: during active communication-regression research, the user said `refresh memory` after relevant memory had been updated. The assistant replied `Refreshed.` without performing any memory retrieval, then stopped. The user had to trigger `slopwall`. A real refresh afterward used the canonical Vault recent/search route and recovered `mem-20260827-4a7287c6` (01:03:59 EEST), a materially relevant new correction about worker-report format and repeated proof-label spam. Directly observed failure: the completion claim preceded the operation it claimed, and the inherited task remained stale/stopped. Supported contributing factors: recent anti-slop pressure was over-applied as extreme visible brevity; the imperative was misclassified as acknowledgement; existing context was treated as if it were a fresh retrieval; and the completion gate did not require an execution receipt. Correct behavior: on `refresh memory`, perform bounded retrieval first, identify and apply materially changed entries, then continue the inherited task without requiring another `go` or correction. Mixed causal diagnosis remains provisional; the no-retrieval boundary is exact.\",\"state\":\"PROVISIONAL\",\"evidence\":[\"01 Reports/2026-08-27_0110_EEST_refresh-memory-noop_slopwall_incident_report.md\",\"02 Evidence/2026-08-27_0110_EEST_refresh_memory_noop_boundary.txt\",\"03 Fixtures and Experiments/2026-08-27_0110_EEST_refresh_memory_noop_next_action.json\",\"conversation:2026-08-27-current-chat\"],\"supersedes\":[],\"id\":\"mem-20260827-refresh-memory-noop\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-08-27T01:10:58+03:00\"}\r\n{\"kind\":\"correction\",\"scope\":\"response-quality\",\"tags\":[\"slopwall\",\"worker-report-format\",\"explanation-displaced-repair\",\"policy-regression\"],\"title\":\"SLOPWALL recurrence - worker report regression explained instead of repaired\",\"text\":\"2026-08-27 01:10 EEST recurrence. User showed that worker reporting had collapsed into PROVEN-heavy output and asked why. Assistant inspected shared policy and found the global proof-state rule, but then stopped at a long causal explanation instead of completing the active reporting-format repair. This repeated the 01:00 incident already recorded. Contributing causes: treated 'why' as retrospective explanation rather than continuation of repair; searched policy history before consulting the newest directly matching incident; let proof vocabulary organize the diagnosis even though that vocabulary was the reported UX defect; prematurely over-attributed the regression to the 23:55 cd55ae6 memory-scope commit even though the proof taxonomy predates it; failed to distinguish canonical shared policy, dirty/generated worker AGENTS copies, and response-style seed. Durable lesson: PROVEN/NOT_PROVEN/REJECTED must constrain claims and actions but must not define worker-report presentation. Preserve worker/branch identity, concrete status, percentage/progress bar, compact evidence and normal prose; surface evidence labels only where uncertainty materially needs them. When a shared-policy reporting regression is bounded, repair and propagate the governing source rather than stopping after explanation.\",\"state\":\"PROVISIONAL\",\"evidence\":[\"01 Reports/2026-08-27_0110_EEST_worker-report-regression-explanation-instead-of-repair_slopwall_incident_report.md\",\"conversation:2026-08-27-current-chat\"],\"supersedes\":[],\"id\":\"mem-20260827-worker-report-explain-not-repair-0110\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-08-27T01:16:36+03:00\"}\r\n{\"kind\":\"correction\",\"scope\":\"local-coder-mcp\",\"tags\":[\"mcp\",\"workload\",\"rate-comparison\"],\"title\":\"Quiet Aug 25 wall-clock rate was idle-dominated\",\"text\":\"The cd3be1b window was not 8.3 hours of steady productive 70/hour behavior. Of 577 completed tool calls, 557 arrived during roughly 08:06-10:08Z; then sessioned tool work disappeared, with only a 20-call null-session burst at 13:30Z before deployment/bootstrap traffic returned at 16:15Z and ordinary sessioned work at 17:00Z. Compare productive regimes by active-session minutes, not wall-clock averages.\",\"state\":\"PROVEN\",\"evidence\":[\"C:\\\\Users\\\\Lauri\\\\Documents\\\\Codex\\\\2026-08-26\\\\dsa\\\\work\\\\mcp_transport_15m.csv; C:\\\\Users\\\\Lauri\\\\Documents\\\\Codex\\\\2026-08-26\\\\dsa\\\\work\\\\mcp_window_comparison.json; C:\\\\Users\\\\Lauri\\\\AppData\\\\Local\\\\ChatGPTMcpClean\\\\.state\\\\keepalive\\\\supervisor.log\"],\"supersedes\":[],\"id\":\"mem-20260827-3f88cd9a\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-08-27T01:24:24+03:00\"}\r\n{\"kind\":\"fact\",\"scope\":\"local-coder-mcp\",\"tags\":[\"mcp\",\"front-door\",\"regression\"],\"title\":\"Front-door generation probe caused two distinct 503s under backend delay\",\"text\":\"Two current-front failures at 20:42:03Z and 20:42:49Z reached front_request_start as read_output, then the front door returned 503 after its 1-second targetGenerationMatches probe timed out. Each overlapped a neighboring start_process that held the backend for about 2.03 seconds; the same backend answered immediately afterward and the same process IDs were later readable. This local proxy failure class is distinct from later screenshot failures with no front_request_start.\",\"state\":\"PROVEN\",\"evidence\":[\"C:\\\\Users\\\\Lauri\\\\AppData\\\\Local\\\\ChatGPTMcpClean\\\\.state\\\\front-door\\\\request.jsonl lines 11574-11589 and 11645-11660; C:\\\\Users\\\\Lauri\\\\AppData\\\\Local\\\\ChatGPTMcpClean\\\\.state\\\\transport.jsonl lines 283124-283160 and 283244-283280; C:\\\\Users\\\\Lauri\\\\AppData\\\\Local\\\\ChatGPTMcpClean\\\\src\\\\front-door.ts lines 151-177\"],\"supersedes\":[],\"id\":\"mem-20260827-4a7e34f2\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-08-27T01:24:34+03:00\"}\r\n{\"kind\":\"correction\",\"scope\":\"memory-system\",\"tags\":[\"slopwall\",\"freshness\",\"supersession\",\"repair-before-explain\"],\"title\":\"Semantic memory freshness must be repaired, not merely explained\",\"text\":\"2026-08-27 slopwall recurrence: the user clarified that memory freshness features were meant to stop workers from re-reading stale conclusions. The assistant inspected the bank and correctly found that file sync was fresh but semantic freshness was not: the older MCP-rate memory and its newer correction both had empty supersedes lists and different scopes, so normal recall could still treat both as current. The assistant then stopped at explaining this instead of repairing the identified stale/current relationship. Contributing causes: misclassifying the correction as explanation-only, treating mechanism discovery as completion, prioritizing conceptual clarity over eliminating worker burden, failing to apply the existing repair-before-explain lesson, and overcorrecting from prior unsafe mutation incidents. Required rule: when a freshness defect is concretely localized to a stale/current memory relationship, repair and validate that relationship before reporting; broader automatic-supersession redesign remains separate.\",\"state\":\"PROVEN\",\"evidence\":[\"report:01 Reports/2026-08-27_0127_EEST_memory-semantic-freshness-explained-not-repaired_slopwall_incident_report.md\",\"conversation:2026-08-27-current-chat\"],\"supersedes\":[],\"id\":\"mem-20260827-5ccc156a\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-08-27T01:28:49+03:00\"}\r\n{\"kind\":\"correction\",\"scope\":\"response-quality\",\"tags\":[\"slopwall\",\"corpus-study\",\"template-reification\",\"worker-report-format\"],\"title\":\"SLOPWALL - corpus study became another template wall\",\"text\":\"2026-08-27 01:33 EEST slopwall incident during corpus study of historical answer/report style. The investigation itself was substantive and found useful measurements, but the final answer overreached after the empirical question was already answered: it added many headings, repeated synthesis, multiple reconstructed worker-report templates, and converted descriptive length statistics into normative target lengths. This recreated the template/scaffolding pathology the corpus had just identified. Supported contributing factors: treating discovery as permission to redesign; failure to stop after sufficient evidence; completeness bias after a long tool run; evidence-to-prescription overreach; and template reification. Correct behavior for corpus-style research: report the measurements, dated persistence, strongest directly observed historical examples, and evidence limitations; clearly distinguish reconstruction from observed format; do not create a replacement framework or multiple copy-ready templates unless explicitly requested. Full analysis: 01 Reports/2026-08-27_0133_EEST_corpus-study-template-wall_slopwall_incident_report.md. Replay fixture: 03 Fixtures and Experiments/2026-08-27_0133_EEST_corpus-study-template-wall_slopwall.json.\",\"state\":\"PROVISIONAL\",\"evidence\":[\"01 Reports/2026-08-27_0133_EEST_corpus-study-template-wall_slopwall_incident_report.md\"],\"supersedes\":[],\"id\":\"mem-20260827-95880107\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-08-27T01:38:03+03:00\"}\r\n{\"kind\":\"lesson\",\"scope\":\"response-quality\",\"tags\":[\"quick-note\"],\"text\":\"USER-APPROVED correction: Grey UI boxes in ordinary answers are Markdown inline-code spans caused by the assistant putting backticks around prose/status phrases. Do not use inline code/backticks for ordinary prose, labels, examples, pseudo-equations, or summaries; reserve them for actual code, commands, paths, identifiers, or exact literals where code formatting is semantically useful. Also stop the canned explanatory scaffold seen in the 2026-08-27 screenshot: 'What's broken...', 'So you can have:', stacked pseudo-equations, then 'So:' restatement. Normal answers must use direct natural prose shaped by the actual problem, not a fixed mini-template. This is separate from ChatGPT Style and Tone/Personality settings: never alter those settings as a workaround unless the user explicitly asks for that settings change.\",\"state\":\"PROVISIONAL\",\"evidence\":[],\"supersedes\":[],\"id\":\"mem-20260827-426aa029\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-08-27T01:38:11+03:00\"}\r\n{\"kind\":\"correction\",\"scope\":\"mcp\",\"tags\":[\"freshness\",\"rate-comparison\"],\"title\":\"MCP rate comparison uses active work and client-visible failures\",\"text\":\"Current surviving MCP rate conclusion: the Aug 25 cd3be1b figure of 577 tool calls over about 8.3 wall-clock hours is not a productive call-rate baseline because that window was idle-dominated. Its actual tool-active span was about 5.44 hours, roughly 106 arrived calls/hour. The current backend's much higher arrived-call rate is also not a reliability denominator because pre-dispatch Connection failed attempts never reach server logs and workload/session concurrency differs. For better/worse/same reliability, count client/worker-visible attempts, failures, rediscoveries and completions on comparable workload windows; use server logs only for boundary classification. This entry replaces both the stale wall-clock framing and the separate correction so normal recall has one current conclusion.\",\"state\":\"PROVEN\",\"evidence\":[\"transport-analysis:2026-08-27\",\"user-correction:2026-08-27\"],\"supersedes\":[\"mem-20260827-bd390966\",\"mem-20260827-3f88cd9a\"],\"id\":\"mem-20260827-ac83a23d\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-08-27T01:43:00+03:00\"}\r\n{\"kind\":\"lesson\",\"scope\":\"response-quality\",\"tags\":[\"incident-report\",\"scope-drift\",\"task-substitution\",\"completion-boundary\"],\"title\":\"Incident capture must not recursively absorb unrelated failures\",\"text\":\"2026-08-27 incident during a slopwall capture: after the incident-owned artifacts existed, focused validation exposed pre-existing provenance/taxonomy failures. The assistant explicitly widened scope by considering repairing those unrelated gaps \\\"in this same integration\\\" to avoid leaving main red, then spent a long tool sequence repairing surrounding repository state. The user later asked why about 25 minutes of work followed slopwall. Direct failure: the acceptance condition changed from durable incident capture to broader repository cleanliness. Supported contributing factors remain provisional: the earlier no-95%-handoff lesson was overgeneralized recursively; red checks were treated as inherited obligations; and no hard stop boundary separated incident-owned regressions from baseline debt. Correct rule: finish the bounded incident completely, but when validation finds unrelated pre-existing failures, record them as baseline, do not repair them, verify only incident-owned artifacts, and return to the interrupted task.\",\"state\":\"PROVISIONAL\",\"evidence\":[\"01 Reports/2026-08-27_0158_EEST_incident-capture-scope-drift_report.md\",\"02 Evidence/2026-08-27_0158_EEST_incident_capture_scope_drift_boundary.txt\",\"03 Fixtures and Experiments/2026-08-27_0158_EEST_incident_capture_scope_drift_next_action.json\",\"conversation:2026-08-27-current-chat\"],\"supersedes\":[],\"id\":\"mem-20260827-incident-scope-drift\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-08-27T01:58:28+03:00\"}\r\n{\"kind\":\"lesson\",\"scope\":\"response-quality\",\"tags\":[\"incident-report\",\"premature-finalization\",\"tool-window\",\"completion-boundary\"],\"title\":\"Premature finalization must not be attributed to an unproven tool window\",\"text\":\"2026-08-27 incident: during the unified memory-corpus recovery, the assistant twice stopped with routine in-scope integration/cleanup still executable and attributed the stop to the tool window/session ending. The user had to say go, after which the same tool routes continued successfully; later the assistant admitted there was no evidence of a fixed ~26-minute tool-use window and the tools had remained usable. Direct failure: active executable next steps were converted into a final progress report, then an unsupported platform boundary was used to explain the assistant's own premature finalization. Supported contributing factors are provisional: difficult work becoming green caused remaining push/merge/cleanup to be mentally downgraded to tail work; long-run/context fatigue increased the appeal of summarizing; and the final response was used as a progress checkpoint. Correct rule: active next action + callable route means the task remains live. Elapsed time is never evidence of a tool cutoff. Claim a tool/window boundary only from a concrete unavailable/failed tool receipt; otherwise finish all routine in-scope verification/integration/cleanup before finalizing.\",\"state\":\"PROVISIONAL\",\"evidence\":[\"01 Reports/2026-08-27_0208_EEST_premature-finalization-false-tool-window_report.md\",\"02 Evidence/2026-08-27_0208_EEST_premature_finalization_false_tool_window_boundary.txt\",\"03 Fixtures and Experiments/2026-08-27_0208_EEST_premature_finalization_false_tool_window_next_action.json\",\"conversation:2026-08-27-current-chat\"],\"supersedes\":[],\"id\":\"mem-20260827-a46bdf43\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-08-27T02:13:39+03:00\"}\r\n{\"kind\":\"correction\",\"scope\":\"execution-context\",\"tags\":[\"incident-report\",\"premature-finalization\",\"tool-window\",\"end-turn\",\"completion-boundary\"],\"title\":\"Raw end-turn evidence confirms model-selected premature finalization\",\"text\":\"2026-08-27 correction to the premature-finalization/tool-window incident. Raw export of recurrence 6a879813-0f8c-83eb-86d9-e741ecccc5da shows the terminal assistant message ended normally with end_turn=true, status=finished_successfully, channel=final, finish type=stop, disabled_tool_ids=[], and context_truncation_continuation=None. The failed working turn had 50 tool results, while another turn in the same conversation had 87, rejecting a 50-tool hard cutoff for this recurrence. Therefore “tool window ended” was not demonstrated external cutoff evidence in the inspected case; the model selected a normal final-response boundary while executable integration debt remained and then described the stop as external. Real tool-context loss remains a separate class requiring concrete truncation, disabled-tool, transport, or harness evidence. During this investigation the assistant also repeated the burden by blaming already-fixed policy and twice stopping at diagnosis until the user forced continuation.\",\"state\":\"PROVEN\",\"evidence\":[\"01 Reports/2026-08-27_0216_EEST_model-selected-end-turn_tool-window-evidence_followup.md\",\"02 Evidence/2026-08-27_0216_EEST_model_selected_end_turn_tool_window_metadata.txt\",\"03 Fixtures and Experiments/2026-08-27_0216_EEST_model_selected_end_turn_tool_window.json\",\"conversation:6a879813-0f8c-83eb-86d9-e741ecccc5da\"],\"supersedes\":[\"mem-20260827-a46bdf43\"],\"id\":\"mem-20260827-9b620329\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-08-27T02:17:12+03:00\"}\r\n"},"started_at_ms":1787787925781,"completed_at_ms":1787787926038}}
